'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  e7-every-hub-width-test.spin2
''   Purpose....  Erratum E7 test: whether a no-wait RDFAST releases
''                RDBYTE, RDWORD, WRBYTE and WRWORD as it does RDLONG and
''                WRLONG; the flags a released read writes, and whether it
''                still steps PTRA++; whether a no-wait WRFAST releases
''                anything; and a SETQ block RDLONG in the window
''   Manual.....  P2 Errata
''   Version....  v0.2.0 (2026-09-26)
''   Appears in.  Erratum E7: After a No-Wait RDFAST, the Next Hub
''                Instruction Can Complete Early; Appendix A: The Test
''                Programs
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Oct 2026
''   Updated....  Oct 2026
''
''   This file is an EXAMPLE from the manual above. It is the whole
''   program the chapters listed above name; where the manual
''   quotes it, it quotes excerpts.
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ WHAT IS KNOWN (Erratum E7, Rev C silicon, 200 MHz)

  After a no-wait RDFAST (D = $8000_0000), a RDLONG issued at once (k = 0
  NOPs between them) that waits for its own hub slot completes early, and
  writes its destination with the long of the PREVIOUS slow hub read (the
  primer), not the long at its own address.  With the primer at slot bits 0
  this happened in 43 of the 64 (af, ar) cells, by delta = (ar - af) mod 8
  as 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2, identical in all 16 repetitions; 7 NOPs (k = 7)
  between the two gave zero.  A WRLONG in the same place was lost when a
  read-back followed (43 cells (old,old), 21 (primer,new)) and landed when
  a NOP followed ((seed,new) in all 64).  The waiting form (D = 0) was
  clean everywhere.

  NAMES USED BELOW AND IN THE PRINTED OUTPUT
    af, ar   the hub slot bits (address bits [4:2]) of the stream address
             and of the test address; aw is the target's slot bits (writes)
    k        the number of NOPs between the RDFAST/WRFAST and the test
             instruction
    C1       NOP control: a NOP stands in for the RDFAST
    PS       stream check: the no-wait RDFAST really starts a stream
    T1       the test: no-wait RDFAST, k NOPs, then the test instruction
    primer   the slow hub read issued just before the RDFAST

WHAT THIS TEST PROGRAM DECIDES, ONE ARM EACH, IN THIS ORDER
  Each arm runs its own controls in the same run and prints its rows, its
  gate and its verdict as soon as it completes, before the next arm starts:
  a crash in a later arm cannot lose an earlier arm's output.  The
  riskiest arm (SETQ block read) runs last.

  ARM 0  POSITIVE CONTROL.  C1, PS, T1 at k = 0 and T1 at k = 7: the basic
         no-wait RDFAST then RDLONG trial of Erratum E7.  MUST reproduce
         the result above, else RIG FAIL and no later verdict counts.
  ARM 1  FLAGS.  T1 at k = 0 with the test instruction "rdlong dst,pr wcz".
         The C and Z flags are captured right after the test instruction
         (WRC + BITZ into a flags register, outside the timed stretch) and
         again after the settle loop (BITC + BITZ, same register), and the
         flags long is written beside the value.  Before every trial the
         flags are preset to C=1 Z=1, which no single read can produce, so
         "flags never written" stays visible.
           FC: primer $A5A5_0001 (bit 31 set, non-zero), sentinel
               $5A5A_0002.  PREDICT released ($A5A5_0001, C=1, Z=0), correct
               ($5A5A_0002, C=0, Z=0).  C decides it.
           FZ: primer $0000_0000, sentinel $5A5A_0002 (non-zero, bit 31
               clear).  PREDICT released ($0000_0000, C=0, Z=1), correct
               ($5A5A_0002, C=0, Z=0).  Z decides it.  The seed $C3C3_0003
               stays non-zero, so "never written" stays visible.  A zero
               record is read as "released" whatever produced it, so the FZ
               verdict also demands T1's exact cell map.
         Each variant: NOP control, waiting form (D = 0) k = 0, test k = 0.
         The flags verdicts name flags the released read did not write (the
         preset survived) and flags that changed after the read (the late
         capture differs); neither ever prints a bare CONFIRMED.
         PTRA++ (records): T1 at k = 0 with the test instruction "rdlong
         dst, ptra++", PTRA set to the test address by a plain "mov ptra,
         pr" before the primer (outside the timed stretch; PTRA's mailbox
         pointer is kept in a register and put back after the command).
         Per record: the value and PTRA after the settle minus PTRA before
         (a correct read gives +4).  NOP control (MUST sentinel, +4),
         waiting form and test; the line "OBSERVED E7 PTRA++:" gives the
         delta distribution split by released / correct cells.  Its test
         run is not gated (it records).
  ARM 2  RDBYTE / RDWORD in place of the test RDLONG (image R shape).
         Primer long $A1B2_C3D4 (four distinct bytes), sentinel table long
         $5A6B_7C8D.  RDBYTE at byte offsets 0, 1, 2, 3 and RDWORD at word
         offsets 0 and 2: offset 0 alone could not tell "shifted by this
         instruction's offset" from "not shifted at all"; offsets 1..3 and
         word offset 2 do, and the four byte offsets cover every byte lane.
         PREDICTION A: a released RDBYTE/RDWORD writes the previous read's
         long ($A1B2_C3D4) shifted right by 8 x its own byte offset and
         masked to its own size, zero-extended:
              RDBYTE offset 0 / 1 / 2 / 3:  $0000_00D4 $0000_00C3
                                            $0000_00B2 $0000_00A1
              RDWORD offset 0 / 2:          $0000_C3D4 $0000_A1B2
         NO RELEASE (the sentinel's part at that offset):
              RDBYTE offset 0 / 1 / 2 / 3:  $0000_008D $0000_007C
                                            $0000_006B $0000_005A
              RDWORD offset 0 / 2:          $0000_7C8D $0000_5A6B
         FLAGS.  The NOP control, the waiting form and the k = 0 test read
         with WCZ and capture the flags exactly as arm 1 (preset C=1 Z=1,
         WRC + BITZ right after the read, BITC + BITZ after the settle).  A
         byte/word read sets C to the MSB of the byte/word and Z if it is
         zero, so each value carries its own flags.  Triples written before
         the run (value, C, Z), released / not released:
              RDBYTE 0: ($D4,1,0) / ($8D,1,0) - same flags: the value decides
              RDBYTE 1: ($C3,1,0) / ($7C,0,0)
              RDBYTE 2: ($B2,1,0) / ($6B,0,0)
              RDBYTE 3: ($A1,1,0) / ($5A,0,0)
              RDWORD 0: ($C3D4,1,0) / ($7C8D,0,0)
              RDWORD 2: ($A1B2,1,0) / ($5A6B,0,0)
         Records are classified by (value, C, Z); the verdicts state the
         flags result.  The k = 7 test records the value only.
         Each variant: NOP control, waiting form k = 0, test k = 0 (PREDICT
         prediction A with its flags in T1's same 43 cells), test k = 7
         (PREDICT none).
  ARM 3  WRBYTE / WRWORD in place of the WRLONG (image W shape).  The
         target long holds old $4C3D_2E1F before every trial; the write
         data register holds $C8D9_EAFB (WRBYTE writes $FB, WRWORD $EAFB).
         Both read-backs are RDLONGs of the aligned long, so a partial write
         is visible.  Same lanes as arm 2.
         PREDICT, as for a released WRLONG: W1 (read-back follows): 43 cells (old,old) - the
         write lost, the target's old long $4C3D_2E1F unchanged - in T1's
         cells, and 21 cells (primer $A5A5_0001, new); W2 (NOP follows):
         (seed,new) in all 64.  NO RELEASE: (new,new), new per lane:
              WRBYTE offset 0 / 1 / 2 / 3:  $4C3D_2EFB $4C3D_FB1F
                                            $4CFB_2E1F $FB3D_2E1F
              WRWORD offset 0 / 2:          $4C3D_EAFB $EAFB_2E1F
         Each variant: NOP control, waiting form W1, test W1, test W2.
  ARM 4  No-wait WRFAST in place of the no-wait RDFAST, then RDLONG (image
         R) and WRLONG (image W, old $0F0F_0004, new $F0F0_0005), at k = 0
         and k = 7, with
         the waiting WRFAST as control.  Runs: image R NOP control, waiting
         WRFAST k=0, no-wait k=0, no-wait k=7; image W NOP control, waiting
         WRFAST W1 k=0, no-wait W1 k=0, W1 k=7, W2 k=0 (W2 tells a lost
         write from a late one).  The image R runs read with WCZ and capture
         the flags as arm 1.  No prediction is made here:
         the arm RECORDS (counts per class and per delta) and its lines say
         OBSERVED, never CONFIRMED or REFUTED.
         A HANG IS A RESULT.  If an arm-4 command does not finish within
         1 s (e.g. the blocking flush never completes after a no-wait
         WRFAST), cog 0 stops the measuring cog (COGSTOP), prints "OBSERVED
         E7 WRFAST: blocking rdfast #0 after a no-wait WRFAST did not
         complete (run <name>)" and the records it has, skips arm 4's
         remaining runs, starts a fresh measuring cog (start-up handshake),
         and goes on to arm 5, which takes its own cog-RAM baseline first.
         FIFO FLUSH.  P2 Documentation, FIFO section: with D[31] = 0 a
         RDFAST or WRFAST "will wait for any previous WRFAST to finish";
         with D[31] = 1 it takes two clocks and does not wait.  So after
         every arm-4 trial, once the settle loop has run, the measuring cog
         issues a blocking "rdfast #0, stream" (waits for any WRFAST to
         finish, then restarts a read stream) and runs a second settle loop.
         Every arm-4 trial therefore starts, like every arm-0 trial, with
         the FIFO in read mode, full and idle, and no write stream pending.
         No WFxxxx is ever issued, so a WRFAST has nothing to write; a stray
         write into the stream region would show as REGION DAMAGE.
  ARM 5  SETQ block RDLONG after a no-wait RDFAST: "setq #7" + "rdlong
         blk0, pr" reads 8 longs into 8 sacrificial cog registers, at k = 0
         and k = 7, waiting form as control.  No prediction is made for
         the block read, so the arm RECORDS.  SETQ must come
         directly before its RDLONG, so here the k NOPs sit between the
         RDFAST and the SETQ, and the RDLONG's command is 2 clocks later
         than in T1 at the same k.
         INTEGRITY.  Before the arm, the measuring cog copies its whole cog
         RAM ($000-$1EF) to hub (SETQ #495 + WRLONG): the baseline, checked
         against the loaded image.  At the end of every arm-5 command it
         copies it again; cog 0 compares, and reports every register that
         changed outside the sacrificial range and outside the loop-variable
         registers (which change by design).  The sacrificial range sits
         between two 8-long guard bands of constants, at the top of the cog
         image, so an overrun in either direction changes a checked register.
         The sacrificial range is preset to the seed before every trial and
         recorded after it, classified per record as: the right block / the
         primer in which longs / seed / other.
         If the measuring cog stops answering, cog 0 stops it (COGSTOP),
         prints "OBSERVED: measuring cog lost during the SETQ block arm" with
         the records it has, then the verdict summary and DEBUG_END_SESSION.
  NOT TESTED: RETA and an interrupt inside the window; hub execution (P2
  Documentation: RDFAST cannot be used in hub execution).

DEBUG
  The program compiles WITH debug (pnut-ts -d) and confines the debugger to
  cog 0 (DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001).  The measuring cog has no debug
  interrupt, no debug() and no BRK, and sets up no interrupt.

SETUP
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  No pins, no jumpers, no instruments.  Cog 0
  (Spin2) fills the hub data, sends one command per run, waits for the
  measuring cog (1 s timeout), classifies the records from hub RAM and
  prints them.  The measuring cog (COGINIT, cog execution, PASM below) runs
  every trial from cog RAM.  Cog 0's Spin2 interpreter uses only the
  blocking RDFAST.  After the records of every command the measuring cog
  writes back the FIFO D value it held (MB_ECHO); a mismatch is RIG FAIL
  and ends the run (after the run's records are printed).

HUB LAYOUT (all below $7_C000; the program image, VAR and cog 0's stack sit
  far below $4_0000, checked at run time before any data is written)
    $4_0000  stream region, 64 longs, long n = $1E1E_0000 + n
    $4_1000  table T: 8 sentinel longs $5A5A_0002, slot bits 0..7
    $4_1100  table B: 8 sentinel longs $5A6B_7C8D (arm 2)
    $4_1200  block source: 15 longs, long i = $5A5A_0100 + i (arm 5)
    $4_2000  image W targets: 8 longs, slot bits 0..7
    $4_3000  primer $A5A5_0001; $4_3020 primer $A1B2_C3D4 (arm 2);
             $4_3040 primer $0000_0000 (arm 1 FZ) - all slot bits 0
    $4_4000  records, up to 8,192 longs (arm 5), to $4_BFFF
    $4_C000  cog-RAM copy, latest (496 longs); $4_D000 the baseline copy
  Every region starts on a 32-byte boundary, so long n has slot bits n mod
  8.  Cog 0 fills the record area with $EEEE_EEEE before every command, so
  a record the measuring cog never wrote is class U.

ONE TRIAL (measuring cog, cog execution; the timed stretch is the primer,
  the RDFAST/WRFAST (or the NOP standing in for it), exactly k NOPs, and the
  test instruction (SETQ + RDLONG in arm 5), adjacent, nothing else, no ##)
  image R:  dst := seed $C3C3_0003 [value + flags: flags := C=1 Z=1]
            [PTRA++: mov ptra, table+4*ar]
            rdlong tmp, primer ; rdfast|wrfast mode, stream+4*af ;
            k x nop ; rdlong|rdbyte|rdword dst, table+4*ar+offset [wcz]
            (PTRA++: rdlong dst, ptra++)
            [value + flags: wrc fl ; bitz fl,#1]  settle (>= 200 clk)
            [arm 4: blocking rdfast #0 + settle]  [value + flags: bitc
            fl,#2 ; bitz fl,#3]  record dst [, fl | , ptra - (table+4*ar)]
  value + flags runs: arm 1 FC/FZ, arm 2 NOP/waiting/k=0, arm 4 image R.
  image W:  wrlong old, target+4*aw ; settle ; rb1 := rb2 := seed
            rdlong tmp, primer ; rdfast|wrfast mode, stream+4*af ; k x nop ;
            wrlong|wrbyte|wrword new, target+4*aw+offset ;
            rdlong rb1, target+4*aw (W1) | nop (W2) ; settle [arm 4: flush]
            rdlong rb2, target+4*aw ; record rb1, rb2
  block:    blk0..blk7 := seed ; rdlong tmp, primer ; rdfast mode, stream+
            4*af ; k x nop ; setq #7 ; rdlong blk0, block+4*ar ; settle ;
            record blk0..blk7 (setq #7 + wrlong)
  16 repetitions x 64 cells per run; record (r*8 + af)*8 + ar.

RECORD CLASSES
  image R  P previous read (the primer; for RDBYTE/RDWORD prediction A's
           part)  S sentinel (its part)  L the primer at ANOTHER offset
           (prediction A's shift wrong)  D seed (never written)
  value + flags   R released (the released value with ITS flags)  S correct
           (the sentinel or its part with ITS flags)  W released value,
           WRONG flags  Q sentinel with the RELEASED flags (where both
           values give the same flags, S wins)  V sentinel with other flags
           L the primer at another offset  D seed
  PTRA++   rows show the value class (image R codes); the PTRA delta (0,
           +4, other) is counted per value group in the run's totals
  image W  per read-back: O old  N new (the lane-merged long)  P primer
           D seed  L old with ANOTHER lane written
  block    . right block  P primer in some longs (rest right)  D seed in
           some longs  M primer and seed  (X other, U unwritten)
  all      F a stream long ($1E1E_0000 + n)  U $EEEE_EEEE (never written)
           X other.  agree: "." all 16 repetitions identical, else the hex
           count identical to repetition 0.
  THE "OTHER" SPLIT.  U in any run fails the arm's gate.  X in a
  NOP control, or in a waiting-form control of arms 1-3 (the waiting
  RDFAST is measured clean), fails it.  X in a test run, or in the
  waiting-form controls of arms 4-5 (never measured), is a result: it is
  named in the verdict.

GATES (printed at the end of each arm)
  RIG FAIL (the test program itself, ends the run): hub layout, run table, timeout in arms
    0-3, mode echo, a restart of the measuring cog failing.  (Arm 4 timeout:
    OBSERVED, restart, on to arm 5.  Arm 5 timeout: OBSERVED, lost cog.)
  ARM 0: "RIG OK (arm 0 ...)" only if C1 sentinel 1024/1024, PS stream long
    1024/1024, T1 k=0 43 primer by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 in every
    repetition (688 primer + 336 sentinel), T1 k=7 sentinel 1024/1024, no
    U, no X, no disagreeing cell.  Else "RIG FAIL (arm 0 ...)", and every
    later verdict prints NO VERDICT.
  ARMS 1-5: "GATE FAIL (arm N)" for: U in any run; a NOP control not clean;
    X as split above; disagreeing repetitions in a control run, or in a
    test run of arms 1-3 (arms 4-5 and the PTRA++ test run record them);
    arm 5's baseline copy not matching the loaded image.  Else "GATES PASS
    (arm N)".  A NO VERDICT caused by disagreeing repetitions in a test run
    adds: "disagreeing repetitions in a test run may be a result: see the
    rows".

VERDICTS (each arm's after its gate; all repeated in the closing summary)
  RIG OK / RIG FAIL                     arm 0
  VERDICT E7 FLAGS C: / FLAGS Z:        NO VERDICT / INCONCLUSIVE (waiting
    form not clean; T not primer-or-sentinel; no release in T) / REFUTED
    (flags not written by the released read; a read's flags not its
    value's) / CONFIRMED (every released record has the predicted flags,
    every correct record its own, 43 per repetition in T1's cells) /
    CONFIRMED AT THE READ, BUT FLAGS CHANGED AFTER THE READ / MECHANISM
    PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS (flags right, cells not T1's)
  OBSERVED E7 PTRA++:                    NO VERDICT or the delta
    distribution split by released / correct cells (records)
  VERDICT E7 RDBYTE: / RDWORD:           NO VERDICT / INCONCLUSIVE (waiting
    form not clean) / REFUTED (seed records; the primer at another offset;
    other or stream values; no release at all; flags not written by the
    released read; flags not the value's) / CONFIRMED (every offset:
    prediction A with its flags in T1's 43 cells per repetition, the rest
    the sentinel part with its flags; k=7 none) / CONFIRMED AT THE READ,
    BUT FLAGS CHANGED AFTER THE READ / MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS.
    Every line also states the k=0 flags result.
  VERDICT E7 WRBYTE: / WRWORD:           NO VERDICT / INCONCLUSIVE (waiting
    form not clean) / REFUTED (writes land after all (W1: old,new);
    released write never lands (W2: rb2 old); defect absent: W1 (new,new)
    everywhere; a pattern not named, incl. another lane written, or no
    lost write) / CONFIRMED (every offset: 43 (old,old) in T1's cells + 21
    (primer,new); W2 (seed,new) 64) / MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS
  OBSERVED E7 WRFAST-RDLONG: / WRFAST-WRLONG: / SETQ-BLOCK:
    NO VERDICT (arm 0 or the arm's gate failed) or "OBSERVED: released
    early in N of 64 cells ..." / "OBSERVED: no early release ...", with
    the class counts, the delta split, (WRFAST-RDLONG) the flags result and
    (SETQ) the integrity result; after an arm 4 hang both WRFAST lines say
    "OBSERVED: blocking rdfast #0 after a no-wait WRFAST did not complete".
  Every byte/word verdict line states both values (with flags for the
  reads) written before the run.

THE MEASURING COG'S IMAGE
  The primer, the RDFAST or WRFAST (or the NOP standing in for it), the k
  NOPs and the test instruction are adjacent instructions in cog RAM, with
  no ## operand between them; the test instruction is followed by the
  capture of the flags or by the read-back, and then by the jump to the
  settle loop.  The only AUGS in the measuring cog is the start-up
  "mov c_tmp, ##STAT_READY", outside every trial; there is no BRK.
  DEBUG OUTPUT.  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub
  strings and numbers and sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in
  ln_out(); the only other record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The
  program therefore carries 2 DEBUG records and a small amount of DEBUG
  data, so it loads and prints.

HOW TO RUN
  Compile with pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or PNut
  Ctrl-F10).  Runs once; nothing written to flash.  Output: header with
  every prediction, then per arm: its runs (rows + totals), its gate line,
  its verdict lines; then the VERDICT SUMMARY and DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY

  NSLOT           = 8                   ' slot bits: address bits [4:2]
  NCELL           = NSLOT * NSLOT       ' (af, ar) cells per repetition
  REPS            = 16                  ' repetitions of every cell per run
  NTRIAL          = REPS * NCELL        ' trials per run (1,024)
  NREC_W          = NTRIAL * 2          ' image W / flags records per run (2,048 longs)
  BLKN            = 8                   ' longs per SETQ block read (setq #BLKN-1)
  NREC_B          = NTRIAL * BLKN       ' block records per run (8,192 longs)
  K_FAR           = 7                   ' the far NOP count: no release from k=7
  SETTLE_N        = 100                 ' DJNZ count of a settle loop: >= 200 clocks
  STREAM_WAIT     = 200                 ' PS: WAITX between the no-wait RDFAST and its RFLONG

  PRIMV           = $A5A5_0001          ' primer (arms 0, 1 FC, 3, 4, 5)
  SENTV           = $5A5A_0002          ' sentinel, table T
  SEEDV           = $C3C3_0003          ' seed: destination before the trial ("never written")
  OLDV            = $0F0F_0004          ' arm 4 image W: the target before the trial
  NEWV            = $F0F0_0005          ' arm 4 image W: what the WRLONG writes
  PRIMB           = $A1B2_C3D4          ' arm 2 primer: four distinct bytes
  SENTB           = $5A6B_7C8D          ' arm 2 sentinel, table B
  PRIMZ           = $0000_0000          ' arm 1 FZ primer
  OLDB            = $4C3D_2E1F          ' arm 3 target before the trial (four distinct bytes)
  NEWD            = $C8D9_EAFB          ' arm 3 write data: WRBYTE writes $FB, WRWORD $EAFB
  BLK_V           = $5A5A_0100          ' block source long i = BLK_V + i
  GUARD_V         = $6D6D_0000          ' cog guard-band long i = GUARD_V + i
  STRM_V          = $1E1E_0000          ' stream region long n = STRM_V + n
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' record-area fill: nothing written here
  FIFO_NO_WAIT    = $8000_0000          ' RDFAST/WRFAST D: D[31]=1 no-wait, block count 0
  FIFO_WAIT       = $0000_0000          ' RDFAST/WRFAST D: D[31]=0 waiting form, block count 0

  T1_PRED         = 43                  ' Erratum E7: primer cells per repetition at k=0
  T1_PRED_SENT    = NCELL - T1_PRED     ' 21
  T3_PRED_OO      = 43                  ' Erratum E7: (old,old) cells per repetition
  T3_PRED_PN      = 21                  ' Erratum E7: (primer,new) cells per repetition

  ' arm 1 flags long: bit 0 C and bit 1 Z right after the test instruction,
  ' bit 2 C and bit 3 Z after the settle loop
  FLB_C_IMM       = 0
  FLB_Z_IMM       = 1
  FLB_C_LATE      = 2
  FLB_Z_LATE      = 3
  FL_PRESET       = %11                 ' C=1 Z=1: preset; no single read gives both

  ' -- fixed hub layout (HUB LAYOUT in the header) --
  HUB_STRM        = $4_0000
  STRM_LONGS      = 64
  HUB_TBL         = $4_1000
  HUB_TBLB        = $4_1100
  HUB_BLK         = $4_1200
  BLK_LONGS       = NSLOT + BLKN - 1    ' 15: blocks start at slot bits 0..7
  HUB_WTBL        = $4_2000
  HUB_PRIM        = $4_3000
  HUB_PRIMB       = $4_3020
  HUB_PRIMZ       = $4_3040
  HUB_RES         = $4_4000
  HUB_DUMP        = $4_C000             ' cog-RAM copy written by the measuring cog
  HUB_DUMP0       = $4_D000             ' the baseline copy (cog 0 moves it here)
  COG_DUMP_N      = $1F0                ' cog registers $000-$1EF (496)
  HUB_DATA_LO     = HUB_STRM
  HUB_DATA_END    = HUB_DUMP0 + COG_DUMP_N * 4
  HUB_TOP16K      = $7_C000
  STACK_MARGIN    = $4000

  STAT_READY      = $0000_0A11
  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars); longer text is cut
  INT_SHOW        = 16                  ' changed cog registers listed per run

  SUCCESS         = 0
  E_RIG_FAIL      = -1                  ' the measuring cog did not answer within 1 s
  E_MODE_FAIL     = -2                  ' the mode echoed back differs from the mode sent

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  #1, CMD_R, CMD_F, CMD_W, CMD_B, CMD_SNAP, CMD_P

  #0, ARM_P, ARM_FL, ARM_RD, ARM_WR, ARM_WF, ARM_Q
  NARM            = ARM_Q + 1

  ' shapes: image R; PS; value + flags (SH_F); image W; block; value + PTRA delta (SH_P)
  #0, SH_R, SH_PS, SH_F, SH_W, SH_B, SH_P
  #0, KD_NOP, KD_PS, KD_WAIT, KD_TEST

  ' trial copies (the measuring cog's vec_tab order)
  #0, CP_R_NOP_L, CP_R_RF0_L, CP_R_RF7_L, CP_R_PS
  #4, CP_R_RF7_B, CP_R_RF7_W
  #6, CP_F_NOP, CP_F_RF0, CP_F_WF0, CP_F_WF7
  #10, CP_FB_NOP, CP_FB_RF0, CP_FW_NOP, CP_FW_RF0
  #14, CP_W_NOP_B, CP_W_RF1_B, CP_W_RF2_B
  #17, CP_W_NOP_W, CP_W_RF1_W, CP_W_RF2_W
  #20, CP_W_NOP_L, CP_W_WF1_L0, CP_W_WF1_L7, CP_W_WF2_L0
  #24, CP_B_NOP, CP_B_RF0, CP_B_RF7
  #27, CP_P_NOP, CP_P_RF0

  ' run-table fields (runTab, 8 bytes per run)
  #0, RF_ARM, RF_SHAPE, RF_KIND, RF_COPY, RF_NOWAIT, RF_K, RF_SIZE, RF_LANE
  RT_W            = 8

  ' run indexes, in run order
  RUN_C1          = 0
  RUN_PS          = 1
  RUN_T1          = 2                   ' T1 k=0: the reference cell map for every arm
  RUN_T1F         = 3                   ' T1 k=7
  RUN_FL          = 4                   ' arm 1: FC N, C, T, then FZ N, C, T, then FP (PTRA++) N, C, T
  RUN_FP          = RUN_FL + 6
  RUN_RD          = RUN_FL + 9          ' arm 2: variant v (0..5) slot j at RUN_RD + 4*v + j
  NVAR            = 6                   ' byte offsets 0..3, word offsets 0, 2
  RUN_WR          = RUN_RD + NVAR * 4   ' arm 3: same layout
  RUN_WF          = RUN_WR + NVAR * 4   ' arm 4 image R: N, C, T k0, T k7
  RUN_WFW         = RUN_WF + 4          ' arm 4 image W: N, C, T1 k0, T1 k7, T2 k0
  RUN_Q           = RUN_WFW + 5         ' arm 5: N, C, T k0, T k7
  NRUN            = RUN_Q + 4
  NBRUN           = 4
  NPRUN           = 3                   ' arm 1 PTRA++ runs: N, C, T
  #0, SL_N, SL_C, SL_T0, SL_T7          ' arm 2 slots (N, C, T0: value + flags; T7: image R)
  #0, SW_N, SW_C, SW_T1, SW_T2          ' arm 3 slots

  ' value classes (image R and W; the flags and block classes share the L/F/U/X slots)
  #0, VC_OLD, VC_NEW, VC_PRIM, VC_SEED, VC_SENT, VC_LANE, VC_SPARE, VC_STRM, VC_UNWR, VC_OTHER
  NVC             = VC_OTHER + 1
  NPAIR           = NVC * NVC
  PAIR_OO         = VC_OLD * NVC + VC_OLD
  PAIR_ON         = VC_OLD * NVC + VC_NEW
  PAIR_NN         = VC_NEW * NVC + VC_NEW
  PAIR_PN         = VC_PRIM * NVC + VC_NEW
  PAIR_DN         = VC_SEED * NVC + VC_NEW
  ' value + flags classes (value, C, Z): arm 1 FC/FZ, arm 2 N/C/T0, arm 4 image R
  #0, FL_REL, FL_OK, FL_REL_WF, FL_OK_RF, FL_OK_WF
  FL_LANE         = VC_LANE             ' the primer's part at another offset
  FL_SEED         = VC_SPARE
  FL_STRM         = VC_STRM
  FL_UNWR         = VC_UNWR
  FL_OTHER        = VC_OTHER
  ' block record classes
  #0, BC_OK, BC_PRIM, BC_SEED, BC_MIX
  BC_UNWR         = VC_UNWR
  BC_OTHER        = VC_OTHER

  ' mailbox longs (cog 0 <-> measuring cog)
  #0, MB_CMD, MB_COPY, MB_MODE, MB_OFF, MB_PRIM, MB_TBL, MB_OLD, MB_NEW, MB_FLUSH, MB_ALIVE, MB_ECHO, MB_LEN

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  long measCog
  byte cellCode[NRUN * NCELL]           ' repetition 0: class (R, F, B) or pair code (W)
  byte cellAgree[NRUN * NCELL]          ' repetitions identical to repetition 0
  long runCnt[NRUN * NVC]               ' classes over all repetitions (W: rb1 and rb2)
  long runRep0[NRUN * NPAIR]            ' repetition-0 cells per code
  long runDelta[NRUN * NSLOT]           ' rep 0 by delta: released cells (R/F: primer value, W: (old,old), B: primer in the record)
  long runDelta2[NRUN * NSLOT]          ' rep 0 by delta: cells not clean
  long runDisagree[NRUN]
  long runGoodAll[NRUN]                 ' over all repetitions: clean records / cells
  long runOther[NRUN]
  long runOtherVal[NRUN]
  long runStrmVal[NRUN]
  long runLaneVal[NRUN]
  long runLate[NRUN]                    ' value + flags runs: flags changed between the two captures
  long runNoFlag[NRUN]                  ' value + flags runs: preset flags C=1 Z=1 survived
  long runFlagVal[NRUN]                 ' value + flags runs: first wrong flags (low 4 bits), -1 none
  long ptrDel[NPRUN * 9]                ' PTRA++ runs: [run][value group: released, correct, other][delta: 0, +4, other]
  long ptrOddDel[NPRUN]                 ' PTRA++ runs: the first delta that is neither 0 nor +4
  long armTestDis[NARM]                 ' disagreeing cells in gated test runs (arms 0-3)
  long wfHang                           ' arm 4: a command timed out (the measuring cog was restarted)
  long wfHangRun
  long blkPrim[NBRUN * BLKN]            ' arm 5: primer, per long index, all reps
  long blkSeed[NBRUN * BLKN]
  long blkOth[NBRUN * BLKN]
  long blkOthVal[NBRUN]
  long blkOthIdx[NBRUN]
  long intChanged[NBRUN]                ' arm 5: changed cog registers, -1 = no copy arrived
  long intFirst[NBRUN]                  ' arm 5: the first changed register
  long armDamage[NARM]
  long armDone[NARM]                    ' the arm finished and its gate was decided
  long armPass[NARM]                    ' its gate passed
  long baseOk
  long bLost
  long lostRun
  ' classification references for the run being processed (set_ref)
  long refArm, refShape, refSize, refLane, refMask, refPrimL, refPrim, refSent
  long refOld, refData, refNew, refRelFl, refOkFl
  ' print buffers
  byte rowStr[NSLOT * 3 + 1]
  byte agreeStr[NSLOT + 1]
  ' every printed line is built here and sent by ONE debug() record (ln_out)
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | armIdx, status, pStack
'' Run the six arms in order on the measuring cog; each prints its runs, its
'' gate and its verdicts when it completes; then the verdict summary.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm (ARM_*)
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the failure that ended the run
' @local pStack - hub address of this method's locals: cog 0's stack

  pStack := @status
  linePos := 0
  ' the layout check runs before the first write to the fixed data area it protects
  if pStack + STACK_MARGIN > HUB_DATA_LO or HUB_DATA_END > HUB_TOP16K
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: hub layout - cog 0 stack at "))
    ln_h(pStack)
    ln_s(string(" must lie at least "))
    ln_h(STACK_MARGIN)
    ln_s(string(" below the data at "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_LO)
    ln_s(string(", and the data end "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
    ln_s(string(" must lie below "))
    ln_h(HUB_TOP16K)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  if @runTabEnd - @runTab <> NRUN * RT_W
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: run table holds "))
    ln_d(@runTabEnd - @runTab)
    ln_s(string(" bytes, expected "))
    ln_d(NRUN * RT_W)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  reset_tallies()
  fill_regions()

  print_header(pStack)

  if start_meas_cog() <> SUCCESS
    finish()

  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARM - 1
    status := run_arm(armIdx)
    if status <> SUCCESS
      quit

  print_summary()
  finish()

PRI start_meas_cog() : status | startCt
' Start a measuring cog (COGINIT, cog execution) and wait for its start-up
' handshake.  Used at start-up and after an arm 4 timeout.  Prints RIG FAIL
' on failure.
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS or E_RIG_FAIL

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT at the start of the start-up timeout

  status := SUCCESS
  mbox[MB_CMD] := 0                     ' a fresh cog must not see a stale command
  mbox[MB_ALIVE] := 0
  measCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if measCog < 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(measCog)
    ln_out()
    status := E_RIG_FAIL
  else
    startCt := getct()
    repeat until mbox[MB_ALIVE] == STAT_READY
      if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
        ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog start-up expected $0000_0A11 within 1 s, got "))
        ln_h(mbox[MB_ALIVE])
        ln_out()
        status := E_RIG_FAIL
        quit
    if status == SUCCESS
      ln_s(string("measuring cog "))
      ln_d(measCog)
      say(string(" running"))

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_d(value) | divisor, bStarted
' Append a signed decimal to the line.
'
' @param value - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  if value == NEGX
    ln_s(string("-2147483648"))
  else
    if value < 0
      ln_c("-")
      value := -value
    divisor := 1_000_000_000
    bStarted := FALSE
    repeat 10
      if value >= divisor or bStarted or divisor == 1
        ln_c("0" + value / divisor)
        value //= divisor
        bStarted := TRUE
      divisor /= 10

PRI ln_hx(value, digits) | idx, nibble
' Append "$" and the low digits hex digits of value.
'
' @param value - the number
' @param digits - hex digits to print (1..8)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, digits-1 .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from digits - 1 to 0
    nibble := (value >> (idx * 4)) & $F
    if nibble < 10
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - 10)

PRI ln_h(value) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param value - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from 7 to 0
    nibble := (value >> (idx * 4)) & $F
    if nibble < 10
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - 10)
    if idx == 4
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_row8(pLongs) | idx
' Append 8 longs as decimals separated by single spaces.
'
' @param pLongs - hub address of the first long

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index 0..7

  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if idx > 0
      ln_c(" ")
    ln_d(long[pLongs][idx])

PRI ln_flags(flagBits)
' Append "C=c Z=z" for a 2-bit flags value (bit 0 C, bit 1 Z).
'
' @param flagBits - the flags

  ln_s(string("C="))
  ln_d(flagBits & 1)
  ln_s(string(" Z="))
  ln_d((flagBits >> 1) & 1)

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' set-up, the run table and the command channel
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header(pStack) | varIdx
' Print the program identity, the layout and every prediction before the run.
'
' @param pStack - hub address of main()'s locals (cog 0's stack)

' Local Variables:
' @local varIdx - arm 2/3 variant

  say(string("=== P2 Errata E7: scope of the no-wait RDFAST early release - flags, RDBYTE/RDWORD, WRBYTE/WRWORD, no-wait WRFAST, SETQ block read (clk 200 MHz) ==="))
  say(string("values: primer $A5A5_0001 / $A1B2_C3D4 (arm 2) / $0000_0000 (arm 1 FZ); sentinel $5A5A_0002 / $5A6B_7C8D (arm 2); seed $C3C3_0003; old $0F0F_0004 new $F0F0_0005 (arm 4)"))
  say(string("values: arm 3 old $4C3D_2E1F data $C8D9_EAFB; block long i $5A5A_0100+i; stream long n $1E1E_0000+n; unwritten $EEEE_EEEE"))
  ln_s(string("hub: stream "))
  ln_h(HUB_STRM)
  ln_s(string(" tables "))
  ln_h(HUB_TBL)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_TBLB)
  ln_s(string(" block "))
  ln_h(HUB_BLK)
  ln_s(string(" targets "))
  ln_h(HUB_WTBL)
  ln_s(string(" primers "))
  ln_h(HUB_PRIM)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_PRIMB)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_PRIMZ)
  ln_s(string(" records "))
  ln_h(HUB_RES)
  ln_s(string(" cog copies "))
  ln_h(HUB_DUMP)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_DUMP0)
  ln_s(string("; data end "))
  ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
  ln_s(string("; measuring-cog image "))
  ln_h(@pasm)
  ln_s(string("; last VAR byte array "))
  ln_h(@lineBuf)
  ln_s(string("; cog 0 stack "))
  ln_h(pStack)
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("measuring cog: image $000-"))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@pasm_end) - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string("; loop variables "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_cmd), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_tmp), 3)
  ln_s(string("; guard bands "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_lo), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_lo) + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string(" and "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_hi), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_hi) + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string("; sacrificial range "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_blk0), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_blk0) + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_out()
  say(string("codes: image R  P previous read (primer / prediction A part)  S sentinel (part)  L primer at another offset  D seed  F stream long  U unwritten  X other"))
  say(string("codes: value+flags  R released (primer/part, its flags)  S correct (sentinel/part, its flags)  W released value wrong flags  Q sentinel released flags  V sentinel other flags  L D F U X"))
  say(string("codes: PTRA++ rows show the value class (P S D F U X); the PTRA delta (after minus before; a correct read gives +4) is in each run's totals"))
  say(string("codes: image W cell rb1 rb2 each  O old  N new  P primer  D seed  L another lane written  F U X | block  . right block  P primer in some longs  D seed in some  M both  X U"))
  say(string("agree: . all 16 identical, else hex count identical to rep 0. delta = (ar - af) mod 8 (image W: aw - af). Every run: 16 repetitions x 64 cells"))
  say(string("ARM 0 MUST (Erratum E7): C1 sentinel 1024; PS stream long 1024; T1 k=0 43 primer per repetition by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 (688 of 1024); T1 k=7 sentinel 1024. Else RIG FAIL: no later verdict counts"))
  say(string("ARM 1 PREDICT: FC released ($A5A5_0001, C=1, Z=0) / correct ($5A5A_0002, C=0, Z=0); FZ released ($0000_0000, C=0, Z=1) / correct ($5A5A_0002, C=0, Z=0); released in T1's 43 cells"))
  say(string("ARM 1 PTRA++ RECORDS (no prediction): rdlong dst,ptra++ at k=0, ptra preset to the test address; ptra after minus before, split by released / correct cells (a correct read: +4)"))
  say(string("ARM 2 PREDICTION A: a released RDBYTE/RDWORD writes the previous read's long $A1B2_C3D4 >> (8 x its own offset), masked to its size, with that value's flags (C = its MSB, Z = zero);"))
  say(string("  in T1's 43 cells at k=0, none at k=7 (k=7 records the value only). Triples written before the run (value, C, Z):"))
  repeat varIdx from 0 to NVAR - 1
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_s(lookupz(varIdx: string("RDBYTE offset 0"), string("RDBYTE offset 1"), string("RDBYTE offset 2"), string("RDBYTE offset 3"), string("RDWORD offset 0"), string("RDWORD offset 2")))
    ln_s(string(": released (prediction A) ("))
    ln_h(part(PRIMB, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)))
    ln_s(string(", "))
    ln_flags(flags_of(part(PRIMB, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)), var_size(varIdx)))
    ln_s(string(") | not released (sentinel part) ("))
    ln_h(part(SENTB, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)))
    ln_s(string(", "))
    ln_flags(flags_of(part(SENTB, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)), var_size(varIdx)))
    ln_c(")")
    if flags_of(part(PRIMB, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)), var_size(varIdx)) == flags_of(part(SENTB, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)), var_size(varIdx))
      ln_s(string(" - same flags: only the value decides here"))
    ln_out()
  say(string("ARM 3 PREDICT (as for a released WRLONG): W1 43 (old,old) in T1's cells (write lost, target stays $4C3D_2E1F) + 21 (primer $A5A5_0001, new); W2 (seed,new) in all 64. Not released: (new,new):"))
  repeat varIdx from 0 to NVAR - 1
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_s(lookupz(varIdx: string("WRBYTE offset 0"), string("WRBYTE offset 1"), string("WRBYTE offset 2"), string("WRBYTE offset 3"), string("WRWORD offset 0"), string("WRWORD offset 2")))
    ln_s(string(": new "))
    ln_h(merge(OLDB, NEWD, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)))
    ln_out()
  say(string("ARM 4 RECORDS (no prediction): no-wait WRFAST then RDLONG wcz (value + flags) / WRLONG, k=0 and k=7, waiting WRFAST control; FIFO flushed after every trial by a blocking rdfast #0 + settle"))
  say(string("ARM 4 on a timeout: the measuring cog is stopped, the arm's remaining runs are skipped, a fresh measuring cog is started and the run goes on to arm 5"))
  say(string("ARM 5 RECORDS (no prediction): no-wait RDFAST / k NOP / setq #7 / rdlong into the sacrificial range, k=0 and k=7, waiting form control; cog-RAM integrity checked after every run"))
  say(string("refuting outcomes: see each arm's header and the VERDICT lines; rig fails: U in any run, a NOP control not clean, X in a control (arms 4-5 waiting forms record it), disagreeing repetitions (arms 4-5 and PTRA++ test runs record them), mode echo"))

PRI fill_regions() | idx
' Write every fixed data region its pattern.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    long[HUB_STRM][idx] := STRM_V + idx
  longfill(HUB_TBL, SENTV, NSLOT)
  longfill(HUB_TBLB, SENTB, NSLOT)
  repeat idx from 0 to BLK_LONGS - 1
    long[HUB_BLK][idx] := BLK_V + idx
  longfill(HUB_WTBL, OLDV, NSLOT)
  long[HUB_PRIM] := PRIMV
  long[HUB_PRIMB] := PRIMB
  long[HUB_PRIMZ] := PRIMZ

PRI region_damage() : damageCnt | idx
' Count read-only data longs that no longer hold their pattern.
'
' @returns damageCnt - changed longs (stream, tables, block source, primers)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  damageCnt := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    if long[HUB_STRM][idx] <> STRM_V + idx
      damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if long[HUB_TBL][idx] <> SENTV
      damageCnt++
    if long[HUB_TBLB][idx] <> SENTB
      damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to BLK_LONGS - 1
    if long[HUB_BLK][idx] <> BLK_V + idx
      damageCnt++
  if long[HUB_PRIM] <> PRIMV
    damageCnt++
  if long[HUB_PRIMB] <> PRIMB
    damageCnt++
  if long[HUB_PRIMZ] <> PRIMZ
    damageCnt++

PRI reset_tallies()
' Clear every tally.
'

  bytefill(@cellCode, 0, NRUN * NCELL)
  bytefill(@cellAgree, 0, NRUN * NCELL)
  longfill(@runCnt, 0, NRUN * NVC)
  longfill(@runRep0, 0, NRUN * NPAIR)
  longfill(@runDelta, 0, NRUN * NSLOT)
  longfill(@runDelta2, 0, NRUN * NSLOT)
  longfill(@runDisagree, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runGoodAll, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOther, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOtherVal, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runStrmVal, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runLaneVal, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runLate, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runNoFlag, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runFlagVal, -1, NRUN)
  longfill(@ptrDel, 0, NPRUN * 9)
  longfill(@ptrOddDel, 0, NPRUN)
  longfill(@armTestDis, 0, NARM)
  wfHang := FALSE
  wfHangRun := -1
  longfill(@blkPrim, 0, NBRUN * BLKN)
  longfill(@blkSeed, 0, NBRUN * BLKN)
  longfill(@blkOth, 0, NBRUN * BLKN)
  longfill(@blkOthVal, 0, NBRUN)
  longfill(@blkOthIdx, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@intChanged, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@intFirst, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@armDamage, 0, NARM)
  longfill(@armDone, FALSE, NARM)
  longfill(@armPass, FALSE, NARM)
  baseOk := FALSE
  bLost := FALSE
  lostRun := -1

PRI run_fld(runIdx, fieldIdx) : value
' @param runIdx - run index
' @param fieldIdx - RF_* field
' @returns value - the run table byte

  value := byte[@runTab][runIdx * RT_W + fieldIdx]

PRI cog_addr(hubAddr) : cogAddr
' @param hubAddr - hub address of a long in the measuring cog's image
' @returns cogAddr - its cog register address

  cogAddr := (hubAddr - @pasm) >> 2

PRI var_size(varIdx) : sizeBytes
' @param varIdx - arm 2/3 variant 0..5
' @returns sizeBytes - 1 (byte offsets 0..3) or 2 (word offsets 0, 2)

  if varIdx < 4
    sizeBytes := 1
  else
    sizeBytes := 2

PRI var_lane(varIdx) : laneIdx
' @param varIdx - arm 2/3 variant 0..5
' @returns laneIdx - the byte offset

  laneIdx := lookupz(varIdx: 0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 2)

PRI flags_of(value, sizeBytes) : flagBits
' The flags a read of value gives with WCZ: C = the MSB of its size, Z = (value == 0).
'
' @param value - the number
' @param sizeBytes - 1, 2 or 4
' @returns flagBits - bit 0 C, bit 1 Z

  flagBits := (value >> (sizeBytes * 8 - 1)) & 1
  if value == 0
    flagBits |= %10

PRI size_mask(sizeBytes) : maskVal
' @param sizeBytes - 1, 2 or 4
' @returns maskVal - $FF, $FFFF or $FFFF_FFFF

  if sizeBytes == 1
    maskVal := $FF
  elseif sizeBytes == 2
    maskVal := $FFFF
  else
    maskVal := $FFFF_FFFF

PRI part(longVal, sizeBytes, laneIdx) : partVal
' The value a byte/word read at byte offset laneIdx of longVal returns
' (shifted and masked; zero-extended).
'
' @param longVal - the long
' @param sizeBytes - 1, 2 or 4
' @param laneIdx - byte offset
' @returns partVal - the part

  partVal := (longVal >> (laneIdx * 8)) & size_mask(sizeBytes)

PRI merge(oldVal, dataVal, sizeBytes, laneIdx) : newVal | maskVal
' The long a byte/word/long write of dataVal at offset laneIdx leaves in oldVal.
'
' @param oldVal - the target long before the write
' @param dataVal - the write data register
' @param sizeBytes - 1, 2 or 4
' @param laneIdx - byte offset
' @returns newVal - the target long after the write

' Local Variables:
' @local maskVal - the size mask

  maskVal := size_mask(sizeBytes)
  newVal := (oldVal & !(maskVal << (laneIdx * 8))) | ((dataVal & maskVal) << (laneIdx * 8))

PRI arm_first(armIdx) : runIdx
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns runIdx - its first run

  runIdx := lookupz(armIdx: RUN_C1, RUN_FL, RUN_RD, RUN_WR, RUN_WF, RUN_Q)

PRI arm_last(armIdx) : runIdx
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns runIdx - its last run

  runIdx := lookupz(armIdx: RUN_FL - 1, RUN_RD - 1, RUN_WR - 1, RUN_WF - 1, RUN_Q - 1, NRUN - 1)

PRI is_w2(copyIdx) : bW2
' @param copyIdx - trial copy
' @returns bW2 - TRUE for a W2 copy (NOP in place of the immediate read-back)

  bW2 := lookdown(copyIdx: CP_W_RF2_B, CP_W_RF2_W, CP_W_WF2_L0) <> 0

PRI is_nop_copy(copyIdx) : bNop
' @param copyIdx - trial copy
' @returns bNop - TRUE when a NOP stands in place of the RDFAST/WRFAST

  bNop := lookdown(copyIdx: CP_R_NOP_L, CP_F_NOP, CP_FB_NOP, CP_FW_NOP, CP_W_NOP_B, CP_W_NOP_W, CP_W_NOP_L, CP_B_NOP, CP_P_NOP) <> 0

PRI is_wf_copy(copyIdx) : bWf
' @param copyIdx - trial copy
' @returns bWf - TRUE for a WRFAST copy

  bWf := lookdown(copyIdx: CP_F_WF0, CP_F_WF7, CP_W_WF1_L0, CP_W_WF1_L7, CP_W_WF2_L0) <> 0

PRI rec_longs(runIdx) : nLongs
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns nLongs - record longs the run writes

  if run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_B
    nLongs := NREC_B
  elseif run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_W or run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_F or run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_P
    nLongs := NREC_W
  else
    nLongs := NTRIAL

PRI send_run(runIdx) : status | shape, armIdx, cmdId, pPrim, pTbl, oldVal, newVal, offVal, modeVal
' Build the command for one run from the run table and send it.
'
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns status - SUCCESS / E_RIG_FAIL / E_MODE_FAIL

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local armIdx - arm
' @local cmdId - CMD_*
' @local pPrim - primer address
' @local pTbl - table / target / block base
' @local oldVal - image W old long
' @local newVal - image W write data
' @local offVal - byte offset
' @local modeVal - FIFO D value

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  armIdx := run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM)
  if shape == SH_B
    cmdId := CMD_B
    pTbl := HUB_BLK
  elseif shape == SH_W
    cmdId := CMD_W
    pTbl := HUB_WTBL
  else
    if shape == SH_F
      cmdId := CMD_F
    elseif shape == SH_P
      cmdId := CMD_P
    else
      cmdId := CMD_R
    if armIdx == ARM_RD
      pTbl := HUB_TBLB
    else
      pTbl := HUB_TBL
  if armIdx == ARM_RD
    pPrim := HUB_PRIMB
  elseif armIdx == ARM_FL and run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE) == 1
    pPrim := HUB_PRIMZ
  else
    pPrim := HUB_PRIM
  if armIdx == ARM_WR
    oldVal := OLDB
    newVal := NEWD
  else
    oldVal := OLDV
    newVal := NEWV
  if armIdx == ARM_RD or armIdx == ARM_WR
    offVal := run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE)
  else
    offVal := 0
  if run_fld(runIdx, RF_NOWAIT)
    modeVal := FIFO_NO_WAIT
  else
    modeVal := FIFO_WAIT
  status := send_cmd(cmdId, run_fld(runIdx, RF_COPY), modeVal, offVal, pPrim, pTbl, oldVal, newVal, armIdx == ARM_WF)

PRI send_cmd(cmdId, copyIdx, modeVal, offVal, pPrim, pTbl, oldVal, newVal, bFlush) : status | startCt
' Hand one command to the measuring cog and wait for it to clear MB_CMD.
'
' @param cmdId - CMD_*
' @param copyIdx - trial copy
' @param modeVal - the RDFAST/WRFAST D value under test
' @param offVal - byte offset added to the test address
' @param pPrim - primer address
' @param pTbl - table / target / block base
' @param oldVal - the target long before the write
' @param newVal - image W write data
' @param bFlush - TRUE: blocking rdfast #0 + settle after every trial (arm 4)
' @returns status - SUCCESS; E_RIG_FAIL on a 1 s timeout; E_MODE_FAIL (after
'   printing its RIG FAIL line) when the mode echoed back is not the mode sent

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the command was issued

  status := SUCCESS
  mbox[MB_COPY] := copyIdx
  mbox[MB_MODE] := modeVal
  mbox[MB_OFF] := offVal
  mbox[MB_PRIM] := pPrim
  mbox[MB_TBL] := pTbl
  mbox[MB_OLD] := oldVal
  mbox[MB_NEW] := newVal
  mbox[MB_FLUSH] := bFlush & 1
  mbox[MB_ECHO] := UNWRITTEN
  mbox[MB_CMD] := cmdId
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_CMD] == 0
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      status := E_RIG_FAIL
      quit
  if status == SUCCESS and mbox[MB_ECHO] <> modeVal
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: command "))
    ln_d(cmdId)
    ln_s(string(" copy "))
    ln_d(copyIdx)
    ln_s(string(" ran with FIFO D "))
    ln_h(mbox[MB_ECHO])
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(modeVal)
    say(string(" (mode echo)"))
    status := E_MODE_FAIL

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' the arm loop
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI run_arm(armIdx) : status | runIdx, damageCnt, bAbort
' Run one arm: its header, every run (rows + totals), its gate, its verdicts.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns status - SUCCESS, or the failure that ends the whole run

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run index
' @local damageCnt - data longs changed by the run just done
' @local bAbort - the arm ended early: no gate, no closing verdicts

  print_arm_header(armIdx)
  status := SUCCESS
  bAbort := FALSE
  if armIdx == ARM_Q
    status := take_baseline()
    bAbort := status <> SUCCESS
  if not bAbort
    repeat runIdx from arm_first(armIdx) to arm_last(armIdx)
      print_run_header(runIdx)
      longfill(HUB_RES, UNWRITTEN, rec_longs(runIdx))
      if run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_B
        longfill(HUB_DUMP, UNWRITTEN, COG_DUMP_N)
      status := send_run(runIdx)
      if status == E_RIG_FAIL
        cogstop(measCog)
        if armIdx == ARM_Q
          bLost := TRUE
          lostRun := runIdx
          say(string("OBSERVED: measuring cog lost during the SETQ block arm"))
          ln_s(string("  the measuring cog did not finish run "))
          ln_runname(runIdx)
          say(string(" within 1 s and was stopped (COGSTOP); the records it wrote before that follow (U = never written)"))
          process_run(runIdx)
          print_run(runIdx)
          observed_q(TRUE)
        elseif armIdx == ARM_WF
          ' arm 4: a hang is a result; restart the measuring cog and go on to arm 5
          wfHang := TRUE
          wfHangRun := runIdx
          ln_s(string("OBSERVED E7 WRFAST: blocking rdfast #0 after a no-wait WRFAST did not complete (run "))
          ln_runname(runIdx)
          say(string(")"))
          ln_s(string("  the measuring cog did not finish run "))
          ln_runname(runIdx)
          say(string(" within 1 s and was stopped (COGSTOP); its records so far follow (U = never written); arm 4's remaining runs are skipped"))
          process_run(runIdx)
          print_run(runIdx)
          status := start_meas_cog()
          if status == SUCCESS
            say(string("  a fresh measuring cog runs arm 5 (arm 5 takes its own cog-RAM baseline first)"))
            print_arm_verdicts(armIdx, FALSE)
        else
          ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not finish run "))
          ln_runname(runIdx)
          say(string(" within 1 s (done flag never cleared); it was stopped (COGSTOP) and the run ends here"))
        bAbort := TRUE
        quit
      process_run(runIdx)
      print_run(runIdx)
      if run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_B
        integrity(runIdx)
      damageCnt := region_damage()
      if damageCnt > 0
        armDamage[armIdx] += damageCnt
        ln_s(string("  REGION DAMAGE after "))
        ln_runname(runIdx)
        ln_s(string(": "))
        ln_d(damageCnt)
        say(string(" read-only data longs changed (a stray hub write) - regions re-filled"))
        fill_regions()
      if status <> SUCCESS
        bAbort := TRUE
        quit
  if not bAbort
    armPass[armIdx] := arm_gate(armIdx)
    armDone[armIdx] := TRUE
    print_arm_verdicts(armIdx, TRUE)

PRI print_arm_header(armIdx)
' @param armIdx - arm

  if armIdx == ARM_P
    say(string("===== ARM 0: POSITIVE CONTROL (C1, PS, T1 k=0, T1 k=7 - the basic Erratum E7 trial; MUST reproduce it, else RIG FAIL and no later verdict counts) ====="))
  elseif armIdx == ARM_FL
    say(string("===== ARM 1: FLAGS ON A RELEASED RDLONG (T1 k=0 with rdlong dst,pr wcz; flags captured right after it and again after the settle); PTRA++ SIDE EFFECT (records) ====="))
  elseif armIdx == ARM_RD
    say(string("===== ARM 2: RDBYTE / RDWORD IN PLACE OF THE TEST RDLONG (prediction A per offset with its flags, printed in the header; k=0 runs read wcz) ====="))
  elseif armIdx == ARM_WR
    say(string("===== ARM 3: WRBYTE / WRWORD IN PLACE OF THE WRLONG (read-back as a long; predicted as for a released WRLONG) ====="))
  elseif armIdx == ARM_WF
    say(string("===== ARM 4: NO-WAIT WRFAST IN PLACE OF THE NO-WAIT RDFAST (RECORDS; RDLONG reads wcz; FIFO flushed after every trial: blocking rdfast #0 + settle) ====="))
  else
    say(string("===== ARM 5: SETQ BLOCK RDLONG AFTER A NO-WAIT RDFAST (RECORDS; runs last; cog-RAM integrity checked after every run) ====="))

PRI take_baseline() : status | addr, imgLen, varLo, varHi, matchCnt, checkCnt
' Arm 5: the measuring cog copies its cog RAM to hub; cog 0 keeps that as the
' baseline and checks it against the loaded image (loop variables excluded).
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS / E_RIG_FAIL / E_MODE_FAIL

' Local Variables:
' @local addr - cog register address
' @local imgLen - registers in the loaded image
' @local varLo - first loop-variable register
' @local varHi - last loop-variable register
' @local matchCnt - image registers equal in the copy
' @local checkCnt - image registers compared

  longfill(HUB_DUMP, UNWRITTEN, COG_DUMP_N)
  status := send_cmd(CMD_SNAP, 0, FIFO_WAIT, 0, HUB_PRIM, HUB_BLK, OLDV, NEWV, FALSE)
  if status == E_RIG_FAIL
    cogstop(measCog)
    say(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not answer the arm 5 baseline command within 1 s; it was stopped (COGSTOP) and the run ends here"))
  if status == SUCCESS
    longmove(HUB_DUMP0, HUB_DUMP, COG_DUMP_N)
    imgLen := cog_addr(@pasm_end)
    varLo := cog_addr(@c_cmd)
    varHi := cog_addr(@c_tmp)
    matchCnt := 0
    checkCnt := 0
    repeat addr from 0 to imgLen - 1
      if addr < varLo or addr > varHi
        checkCnt++
        if long[HUB_DUMP0][addr] == long[@pasm][addr]
          matchCnt++
    baseOk := matchCnt == checkCnt
    ln_s(string("INTEGRITY BASELINE: the measuring cog copied cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub "))
    ln_h(HUB_DUMP)
    ln_s(string(" (kept at "))
    ln_h(HUB_DUMP0)
    ln_s(string("); it equals the loaded image in "))
    ln_d(matchCnt)
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(checkCnt)
    say(string(" image registers outside the loop variables (MUST be all)"))

PRI integrity(runIdx) | bIdx, addr, changed, sacLo, varLo, varHi, checkCnt
' Arm 5: compare the copy written at the end of the run with the baseline;
' print every changed register outside the sacrificial range and the loop
' variables (the first INT_SHOW of them) and the count.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local bIdx - arm 5 run slot
' @local addr - cog register address
' @local changed - changed registers
' @local sacLo - first sacrificial register
' @local varLo - first loop-variable register
' @local varHi - last loop-variable register
' @local checkCnt - registers compared

  bIdx := runIdx - RUN_Q
  if long[HUB_DUMP][0] == UNWRITTEN and long[HUB_DUMP][COG_DUMP_N - 1] == UNWRITTEN
    intChanged[bIdx] := -1
    ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
    ln_runname(runIdx)
    say(string(": no cog-RAM copy arrived (the copy area still holds $EEEE_EEEE)"))
  else
    sacLo := cog_addr(@c_blk0)
    varLo := cog_addr(@c_cmd)
    varHi := cog_addr(@c_tmp)
    changed := 0
    checkCnt := 0
    repeat addr from 0 to COG_DUMP_N - 1
      if (addr < sacLo or addr > sacLo + BLKN - 1) and (addr < varLo or addr > varHi)
        checkCnt++
        if long[HUB_DUMP][addr] <> long[HUB_DUMP0][addr]
          changed++
          if changed == 1
            intFirst[bIdx] := addr
          if changed <= INT_SHOW
            ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
            ln_runname(runIdx)
            ln_s(string(": cog register "))
            ln_hx(addr, 3)
            ln_s(string(" changed: baseline "))
            ln_h(long[HUB_DUMP0][addr])
            ln_s(string(" now "))
            ln_h(long[HUB_DUMP][addr])
            ln_out()
    intChanged[bIdx] := changed
    ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
    ln_runname(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(": "))
    ln_d(changed)
    ln_s(string(" of "))
    ln_d(checkCnt)
    ln_s(string(" cog registers outside the sacrificial range "))
    ln_hx(sacLo, 3)
    ln_c("-")
    ln_hx(sacLo + BLKN - 1, 3)
    ln_s(string(" and the loop variables "))
    ln_hx(varLo, 3)
    ln_c("-")
    ln_hx(varHi, 3)
    say(string(" changed since the baseline"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' classification
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI set_ref(runIdx)
' Set the classification references for one run.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

  refArm := run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM)
  refShape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  refSize := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SIZE)
  refMask := size_mask(refSize)
  if refArm == ARM_RD or refArm == ARM_WR
    refLane := run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE)
  else
    refLane := 0
  if refArm == ARM_RD
    refPrimL := PRIMB
    refSent := part(SENTB, refSize, refLane)
  else
    refPrimL := PRIMV
    refSent := SENTV
  if refArm == ARM_FL and run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE) == 1
    refPrimL := PRIMZ
  refPrim := part(refPrimL, refSize, refLane)
  if refArm == ARM_WR
    refOld := OLDB
    refData := NEWD
  else
    refOld := OLDV
    refData := NEWV
  refNew := merge(refOld, refData, refSize, refLane)
  ' the flags a read of each value gives: C = the MSB of the read's size, Z = (value == 0)
  refRelFl := flags_of(refPrim, refSize)
  refOkFl := flags_of(refSent, refSize)

PRI class_rest(datum) : cls
' The classes shared by every shape after its own values.
'
' @param datum - a record long
' @returns cls - VC_UNWR / VC_STRM / VC_OTHER

  if datum == UNWRITTEN
    cls := VC_UNWR
  elseif (datum - STRM_V) +< STRM_LONGS
    cls := VC_STRM
  else
    cls := VC_OTHER

PRI is_lane_r(datum) : bLane | laneIdx
' @param datum - a record long
' @returns bLane - TRUE when it is the primer's part at ANOTHER offset

' Local Variables:
' @local laneIdx - byte offset 0..3

  bLane := FALSE
  repeat laneIdx from 0 to 3
    if laneIdx <> refLane and datum == part(refPrimL, refSize, laneIdx)
      bLane := TRUE

PRI is_lane_w(datum) : bLane | laneIdx
' @param datum - a record long
' @returns bLane - TRUE when it is the old long with ANOTHER lane written

' Local Variables:
' @local laneIdx - byte offset

  bLane := FALSE
  repeat laneIdx from 0 to 4 - refSize
    if laneIdx <> refLane and datum == merge(refOld, refData, refSize, laneIdx)
      bLane := TRUE

PRI class_v(datum) : cls
' Image R and image W classification against the current references.
'
' @param datum - a record long
' @returns cls - VC_*

  if refShape == SH_W
    if datum == refOld
      cls := VC_OLD
    elseif datum == refNew
      cls := VC_NEW
    elseif datum == PRIMV
      cls := VC_PRIM
    elseif datum == SEEDV
      cls := VC_SEED
    elseif refSize < 4 and is_lane_w(datum)
      cls := VC_LANE
    else
      cls := class_rest(datum)
  else
    if datum == refPrim
      cls := VC_PRIM
    elseif datum == refSent
      cls := VC_SENT
    elseif datum == SEEDV
      cls := VC_SEED
    elseif refSize < 4 and is_lane_r(datum)
      cls := VC_LANE
    else
      cls := class_rest(datum)

PRI class_f(datum, flagLong) : cls | flagImm
' Value + flags runs: classify by the (value, C, Z) triple, flags as
' captured right after the test instruction.  The released value's flags
' (refRelFl) and the correct value's flags (refOkFl) are those a read of
' that value gives; where both are equal the correct class wins.
'
' @param datum - a record long
' @param flagLong - the flags long
' @returns cls - FL_*

' Local Variables:
' @local flagImm - bit 0 C, bit 1 Z, right after the test instruction

  flagImm := flagLong & %11
  if datum == UNWRITTEN
    cls := FL_UNWR
  elseif datum == refPrim
    if flagImm == refRelFl
      cls := FL_REL
    else
      cls := FL_REL_WF
  elseif datum == refSent
    if flagImm == refOkFl
      cls := FL_OK
    elseif flagImm == refRelFl
      cls := FL_OK_RF
    else
      cls := FL_OK_WF
  elseif datum == SEEDV
    cls := FL_SEED
  elseif refSize < 4 and is_lane_r(datum)
    cls := FL_LANE
  else
    cls := class_rest(datum)

PRI vcchar(cls) : codeChar
' @param cls - VC_*
' @returns codeChar - O N P D S L ? F U X

  codeChar := lookupz(cls: "O", "N", "P", "D", "S", "L", "?", "F", "U", "X")

PRI flchar(flClass) : codeChar
' @param flClass - FL_* (L D F U X in the shared slots)
' @returns codeChar - R S W Q V L D F U X

  codeChar := lookupz(flClass: "R", "S", "W", "Q", "V", "L", "D", "F", "U", "X")

PRI bcchar(blkClass) : codeChar
' @param blkClass - BC_* (U X in the shared slots)
' @returns codeChar - . P D M ? ? ? ? U X

  codeChar := lookupz(blkClass: ".", "P", "D", "M", "?", "?", "?", "?", "U", "X")

PRI agreechar(agreeCnt) : codeChar
' @param agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0 (1..16)
' @returns codeChar - "." for all 16, else the hex digit

  if agreeCnt == REPS
    codeChar := "."
  elseif agreeCnt < 10
    codeChar := "0" + agreeCnt
  else
    codeChar := "A" + agreeCnt - 10

PRI cell_delta(cellIdx) : deltaIdx
' @param cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @returns deltaIdx - (ar - af) mod 8

  deltaIdx := ((cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1)) - (cellIdx >> 3)) & (NSLOT - 1)

PRI note_value(runIdx, cls, datum)
' Count one classified value; keep the run's first X, F and L values.
'
' @param runIdx - run index
' @param cls - VC_*
' @param datum - a record long

  if cls == VC_STRM and runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_STRM] == 0
    runStrmVal[runIdx] := datum
  if cls == VC_LANE and runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_LANE] == 0 and refShape <> SH_B
    runLaneVal[runIdx] := datum
  runCnt[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
  if cls == VC_OTHER
    if runOther[runIdx] == 0
      runOtherVal[runIdx] := datum
    runOther[runIdx]++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' processing one run
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI process_run(runIdx)
' @param runIdx - run index

  set_ref(runIdx)
  if refShape == SH_PS
    process_ps(runIdx)
  elseif refShape == SH_R
    process_r(runIdx)
  elseif refShape == SH_F
    process_f(runIdx)
  elseif refShape == SH_W
    process_w(runIdx)
  elseif refShape == SH_P
    process_p(runIdx)
  else
    process_b(runIdx)

PRI process_p(runIdx) | pIdx, cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, firstDel, datum, delta, cls, grp, bucket, agreeCnt, recIdx
' Classify an arm 1 PTRA++ run: value class per record, and the PTRA delta
' (after minus before) by value group (released / correct / other).
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local pIdx - PTRA++ run slot 0..2
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's value
' @local firstDel - repetition 0's delta
' @local datum - a value
' @local delta - its PTRA delta
' @local cls - VC_*
' @local grp - 0 released (primer), 1 correct (sentinel), 2 other
' @local bucket - 0 delta 0, 1 delta +4, 2 other delta
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0 (value and delta)
' @local recIdx - trial index (record pair 2*recIdx, 2*recIdx+1)

  pIdx := runIdx - RUN_FP
  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx]
    firstDel := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx + 1]
    cls := class_v(firstVal)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + cls]++
    if cls == VC_PRIM
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if cls <> VC_SENT or firstDel <> 4
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      recIdx := repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx
      datum := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx]
      delta := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx + 1]
      cls := class_v(datum)
      note_value(runIdx, cls, datum)
      if cls == VC_PRIM
        grp := 0
      elseif cls == VC_SENT
        grp := 1
      else
        grp := 2
      if delta == 0
        bucket := 0
      elseif delta == 4
        bucket := 1
      else
        bucket := 2
        if ptrOddDel[pIdx] == 0
          ptrOddDel[pIdx] := delta
      ptrDel[pIdx * 9 + grp * 3 + bucket]++
      if cls == VC_SENT and delta == 4
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if datum == firstVal and delta == firstDel
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI process_r(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, datum, cls, agreeCnt
' Classify an image R run: repetition-0 codes, agreement, totals, delta split.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's record
' @local datum - a record
' @local cls - its class
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][cellIdx]
    cls := class_v(firstVal)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + cls]++
    if cls == VC_PRIM
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if cls <> VC_SENT
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      datum := long[HUB_RES][repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]
      cls := class_v(datum)
      note_value(runIdx, cls, datum)
      if cls == VC_SENT
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if datum == firstVal
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI process_ps(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, datum, agreeCnt, expVal
' Classify the PS run: every record must be the stream's first long, STRM_V + af.
' Cell code 1 = right, 0 = wrong.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's record
' @local datum - a record
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local expVal - the stream's first long for this af

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    expVal := STRM_V + (cellIdx >> 3)
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][cellIdx]
    if firstVal == expVal
      cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := 1
    else
      cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := 0
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      datum := long[HUB_RES][repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]
      if datum == expVal
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      elseif runOtherVal[runIdx] == 0
        runOtherVal[runIdx] := datum
      if datum == UNWRITTEN
        runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_UNWR]++
      if datum == firstVal
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI process_f(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, firstFl, datum, flagLong, cls, agreeCnt, recIdx
' Classify an arm 1 run by (value, C, Z); count late flag changes.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's value
' @local firstFl - repetition 0's flags long
' @local datum - a value
' @local flagLong - its flags long
' @local cls - FL_*
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0 (value and flags)
' @local recIdx - trial index (record pair 2*recIdx, 2*recIdx+1)

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx]
    firstFl := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx + 1]
    cls := class_f(firstVal, firstFl)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + cls]++
    if cls == FL_REL or cls == FL_REL_WF
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if cls <> FL_OK
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      recIdx := repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx
      datum := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx]
      flagLong := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx + 1]
      cls := class_f(datum, flagLong)
      note_value(runIdx, cls, datum)
      if cls == FL_OK
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if datum <> UNWRITTEN
        if (flagLong & %11) <> ((flagLong >> FLB_C_LATE) & %11)
          runLate[runIdx]++
        if (flagLong & %11) == FL_PRESET
          runNoFlag[runIdx]++
      if (cls == FL_REL_WF or cls == FL_OK_RF or cls == FL_OK_WF) and runFlagVal[runIdx] == -1
        runFlagVal[runIdx] := flagLong & %1111
      if datum == firstVal and flagLong == firstFl
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI process_w(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstRb1, firstRb2, rb1, rb2, pairCode, agreeCnt, recIdx
' Classify an image W run: repetition-0 pair codes, agreement, totals, delta split.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + aw
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstRb1 - repetition 0's rb1
' @local firstRb2 - repetition 0's rb2
' @local rb1 - immediate read-back
' @local rb2 - settled read-back
' @local pairCode - class(rb1) * NVC + class(rb2)
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local recIdx - trial index (record pair 2*recIdx, 2*recIdx+1)

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstRb1 := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx]
    firstRb2 := long[HUB_RES][2 * cellIdx + 1]
    pairCode := class_v(firstRb1) * NVC + class_v(firstRb2)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := pairCode
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + pairCode]++
    if pairCode == PAIR_OO
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if pairCode <> PAIR_NN
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      recIdx := repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx
      rb1 := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx]
      rb2 := long[HUB_RES][2 * recIdx + 1]
      note_value(runIdx, class_v(rb1), rb1)
      note_value(runIdx, class_v(rb2), rb2)
      if rb1 == refNew and rb2 == refNew
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if rb1 == firstRb1 and rb2 == firstRb2
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI class_blk(pRec, arIdx, bIdx, bTally) : cls | longIdx, datum, nPrim, nSeed, nOth, nUnwr
' Arm 5: classify one 8-long record against the block expected for ar.
'
' @param pRec - hub address of the record
' @param arIdx - the block's first slot bits (its first long is block long ar)
' @param bIdx - arm 5 run slot
' @param bTally - TRUE: count per long index
' @returns cls - BC_*

' Local Variables:
' @local longIdx - long index in the record
' @local datum - the long
' @local nPrim - longs holding the primer
' @local nSeed - longs holding the seed
' @local nOth - longs holding anything else
' @local nUnwr - longs holding the record-area fill

  nPrim := 0
  nSeed := 0
  nOth := 0
  nUnwr := 0
  repeat longIdx from 0 to BLKN - 1
    datum := long[pRec][longIdx]
    if datum == BLK_V + arIdx + longIdx
      next
    if datum == PRIMV
      nPrim++
      if bTally
        blkPrim[bIdx * BLKN + longIdx]++
    elseif datum == SEEDV
      nSeed++
      if bTally
        blkSeed[bIdx * BLKN + longIdx]++
    elseif datum == UNWRITTEN
      nUnwr++
    else
      nOth++
      if bTally
        blkOth[bIdx * BLKN + longIdx]++
        if blkOthIdx[bIdx] == -1
          blkOthIdx[bIdx] := longIdx
          blkOthVal[bIdx] := datum
  if nUnwr > 0
    cls := BC_UNWR
  elseif nOth > 0
    cls := BC_OTHER
  elseif nPrim > 0 and nSeed > 0
    cls := BC_MIX
  elseif nPrim > 0
    cls := BC_PRIM
  elseif nSeed > 0
    cls := BC_SEED
  else
    cls := BC_OK

PRI same_block(pRecA, pRecB) : bSame | longIdx
' @param pRecA - a record
' @param pRecB - another record
' @returns bSame - TRUE when all 8 longs are equal

' Local Variables:
' @local longIdx - long index

  bSame := TRUE
  repeat longIdx from 0 to BLKN - 1
    if long[pRecA][longIdx] <> long[pRecB][longIdx]
      bSame := FALSE

PRI process_b(runIdx) | bIdx, cellIdx, repIdx, pRec0, pRec, cls, agreeCnt
' Classify an arm 5 run: per-record classes, per-long counts, agreement.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local bIdx - arm 5 run slot
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local pRec0 - repetition 0's record
' @local pRec - a record
' @local cls - BC_*
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0

  bIdx := runIdx - RUN_Q
  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    pRec0 := HUB_RES + cellIdx * BLKN * 4
    cls := class_blk(pRec0, cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1), bIdx, FALSE)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + cls]++
    if cls == BC_PRIM or cls == BC_MIX
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if cls <> BC_OK
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      pRec := HUB_RES + (repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx) * BLKN * 4
      cls := class_blk(pRec, cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1), bIdx, TRUE)
      runCnt[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
      if cls == BC_OTHER
        runOther[runIdx]++
      if cls == BC_OK
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if same_block(pRec, pRec0)
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' printing one run
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_runname(runIdx) | armIdx, kind, shape
' Append the run's printable name, e.g. "T1 k0", "RB2 T k7", "FW T2 k0".
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local shape - SH_*

  armIdx := run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM)
  kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  if armIdx == ARM_P
    ln_s(lookupz(runIdx: string("C1"), string("PS"), string("T1"), string("T1")))
  else
    if armIdx == ARM_FL
      ln_s(lookupz(run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE): string("FC"), string("FZ"), string("FP")))
    elseif armIdx == ARM_RD
      ln_s(lookupz(run_fld(runIdx, RF_SIZE) >> 1: string("RB"), string("RW")))
      ln_d(run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE))
    elseif armIdx == ARM_WR
      ln_s(lookupz(run_fld(runIdx, RF_SIZE) >> 1: string("WB"), string("WW")))
      ln_d(run_fld(runIdx, RF_LANE))
    elseif armIdx == ARM_WF
      if shape == SH_W
        ln_s(string("FW"))
      else
        ln_s(string("FR"))
    else
      ln_s(string("QB"))
    ln_c(" ")
    if kind == KD_NOP
      ln_c("N")
    elseif kind == KD_WAIT
      ln_c("C")
    elseif shape == SH_W
      if is_w2(run_fld(runIdx, RF_COPY))
        ln_s(string("T2"))
      else
        ln_s(string("T1"))
    else
      ln_c("T")
  ln_s(string(" k"))
  ln_d(run_fld(runIdx, RF_K))

PRI ln_opname(runIdx) | shape, sizeBytes
' Append the test instruction's mnemonic.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local sizeBytes - access size

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  sizeBytes := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SIZE)
  if shape == SH_W
    ln_s(lookupz(sizeBytes >> 1: string("wrbyte"), string("wrword"), string("wrlong")))
  else
    ln_s(lookupz(sizeBytes >> 1: string("rdbyte"), string("rdword"), string("rdlong")))

PRI print_run_header(runIdx) | shape, kind, copyIdx, armIdx
' Print the run's sequence, and its MUST / PREDICT / RECORDS line, before its rows.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local copyIdx - CP_*
' @local armIdx - arm

  set_ref(runIdx)
  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
  copyIdx := run_fld(runIdx, RF_COPY)
  armIdx := run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM)
  ln_s(string("RUN "))
  ln_runname(runIdx)
  ln_s(string(" ("))
  ln_s(lookupz(kind: string("NOP CONTROL"), string("POSITIVE CONTROL"), string("WAITING FORM"), string("TEST")))
  ln_s(string("): rdlong primer "))
  ln_h(refPrimL)
  ln_s(string(" / "))
  if shape == SH_PS
    ln_s(string("rdfast D=$8000_0000 / waitx #200 / rflong"))
  else
    if is_nop_copy(copyIdx)
      ln_s(string("NOP in place of the RDFAST"))
    else
      if is_wf_copy(copyIdx)
        ln_s(string("wrfast D="))
      else
        ln_s(string("rdfast D="))
      if run_fld(runIdx, RF_NOWAIT)
        ln_h(FIFO_NO_WAIT)
      else
        ln_h(FIFO_WAIT)
    ln_s(string(" / "))
    ln_d(run_fld(runIdx, RF_K))
    ln_s(string(" NOP / "))
    if shape == SH_B
      ln_s(string("setq #7 / rdlong block of 8 longs into the sacrificial registers"))
    elseif shape == SH_W
      ln_opname(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" new at offset "))
      ln_d(refLane)
      if is_w2(copyIdx)
        ln_s(string(" / NOP ... rdlong rb2"))
      else
        ln_s(string(" / rdlong rb1 ... rdlong rb2"))
    elseif shape == SH_P
      ln_s(string("rdlong test,ptra++ (ptra := the test address before the primer) ... record ptra after minus before"))
    else
      ln_opname(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" test"))
      if shape == SH_F
        ln_s(string(" wcz / wrc fl / bitz fl ... bitc/bitz fl (late)"))
      if refSize < 4
        ln_s(string(" at offset "))
        ln_d(refLane)
  if armIdx == ARM_WF
    ln_s(string("; every trial ends: settle / rdfast #0 (blocking) / settle"))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("    "))
  ln_expect(runIdx)
  ln_out()

PRI ln_expect(runIdx) | shape, kind, armIdx
' Append the run's MUST / PREDICT / RECORDS statement (references already set).
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local armIdx - arm

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
  armIdx := run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM)
  if kind == KD_PS
    ln_s(string("MUST: the stream's first long $1E1E_0000+af in all 1024 records, else RIG FAIL (the RDFAST under test would not be starting a stream)"))
  elseif kind == KD_NOP
    if shape == SH_W
      ln_s(string("MUST: (new,new), new "))
      ln_h(refNew)
      ln_s(string(", in all 1024 cells, else the arm's gate fails"))
    elseif shape == SH_B
      ln_s(string("MUST: the block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024 records, else the arm's gate fails"))
    elseif shape == SH_F
      ln_s(string("MUST: (sentinel "))
      ln_h(refSent)
      ln_s(string(", "))
      ln_flags(refOkFl)
      ln_s(string(") in all 1024 records, else the arm's gate fails"))
    elseif shape == SH_P
      ln_s(string("MUST: sentinel $5A5A_0002 with ptra +4 in all 1024 records, else the arm's gate fails"))
    else
      ln_s(string("MUST: sentinel "))
      ln_h(refSent)
      ln_s(string(" in all 1024 records, else "))
      if armIdx == ARM_P
        ln_s(string("RIG FAIL"))
      else
        ln_s(string("the arm's gate fails"))
  elseif kind == KD_WAIT
    if armIdx == ARM_WF or armIdx == ARM_Q
      ln_s(string("RECORDS: no prediction (this waiting form was never measured)"))
    elseif shape == SH_W
      ln_s(string("PREDICT: (new,new), new "))
      ln_h(refNew)
      ln_s(string(", in every cell; any other = the waiting form fails"))
    elseif shape == SH_F
      ln_s(string("PREDICT: (sentinel "))
      ln_h(refSent)
      ln_s(string(", "))
      ln_flags(refOkFl)
      ln_s(string(") in every record"))
    elseif shape == SH_P
      ln_s(string("RECORDS: value and ptra delta (a correct read: sentinel, +4); an X value here fails the arm's gate"))
    else
      ln_s(string("PREDICT: sentinel part "))
      ln_h(refSent)
      ln_s(string(" in all 1024 records"))
  else
    if armIdx == ARM_P
      if run_fld(runIdx, RF_K) == 0
        ln_s(string("MUST (Erratum E7): 43 primer per repetition, by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2; every other record sentinel"))
      else
        ln_s(string("MUST (Erratum E7): sentinel in all 1024 records"))
    elseif shape == SH_P
      ln_s(string("RECORDS: no prediction - value class and ptra delta per cell, split by released / correct cells (a correct read: sentinel, +4)"))
    elseif armIdx == ARM_FL or (armIdx == ARM_RD and shape == SH_F)
      ln_s(string("PREDICT per repetition: released ("))
      ln_h(refPrim)
      ln_s(string(", "))
      ln_flags(refRelFl)
      ln_s(string(") in T1's 43 cells; correct ("))
      ln_h(refSent)
      ln_s(string(", "))
      ln_flags(refOkFl)
      ln_s(string(") in the rest"))
    elseif armIdx == ARM_RD
      if run_fld(runIdx, RF_K) == 0
        ln_s(string("PREDICT per repetition: prediction A "))
        ln_h(refPrim)
        ln_s(string(" in T1's 43 cells, sentinel part "))
        ln_h(refSent)
        ln_s(string(" in the rest"))
      else
        ln_s(string("PREDICT: sentinel part "))
        ln_h(refSent)
        ln_s(string(" in all 1024 records (k=7: no release)"))
    elseif armIdx == ARM_WR
      if is_w2(run_fld(runIdx, RF_COPY))
        ln_s(string("PREDICT: (seed,new) in all 64 cells, new "))
        ln_h(refNew)
        ln_s(string("; rb2 old = the released write never lands"))
      else
        ln_s(string("PREDICT per repetition: 43 (old,old) in T1's cells (old "))
        ln_h(refOld)
        ln_s(string(" unchanged: write lost) + 21 (primer $A5A5_0001, new "))
        ln_h(refNew)
        ln_s(string("); (old,new) = write late, not lost"))
    else
      ln_s(string("RECORDS: no prediction"))

PRI print_run(runIdx) | afIdx, arIdx, cellIdx, pairCode, shape
' Print a run's raw rows (repetition 0 per af, agreement) and its totals.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local afIdx - stream slot bits
' @local arIdx - test-address slot bits
' @local cellIdx - index into the per-cell arrays
' @local pairCode - image W cell code
' @local shape - SH_*

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  repeat afIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    repeat arIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
      cellIdx := runIdx * NCELL + afIdx * NSLOT + arIdx
      agreeStr[arIdx] := agreechar(cellAgree[cellIdx])
      if shape == SH_PS
        rowStr[arIdx] := lookupz(cellCode[cellIdx]: "X", ".")
      elseif shape == SH_R or shape == SH_P
        rowStr[arIdx] := vcchar(cellCode[cellIdx])
      elseif shape == SH_F
        rowStr[arIdx] := flchar(cellCode[cellIdx])
      elseif shape == SH_B
        rowStr[arIdx] := bcchar(cellCode[cellIdx])
      else
        pairCode := cellCode[cellIdx]
        rowStr[arIdx * 3] := vcchar(pairCode / NVC)
        rowStr[arIdx * 3 + 1] := vcchar(pairCode // NVC)
        rowStr[arIdx * 3 + 2] := " "
    agreeStr[NSLOT] := 0
    if shape == SH_W
      rowStr[NSLOT * 3 - 1] := 0
    else
      rowStr[NSLOT] := 0
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_runname(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" af"))
    ln_d(afIdx)
    ln_s(string(" rep0 a0-7: "))
    ln_s(@rowStr)
    ln_s(string("  agree "))
    say(@agreeStr)
  print_totals(runIdx)

PRI ln_lead(runIdx)
' Append "  <run name>", the lead of every per-run total line.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_runname(runIdx)

PRI print_totals(runIdx) | base, shape, bIdx
' Print a run's totals: classes over all repetitions, repetition-0 delta splits.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local base - index of the run's first class count
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local bIdx - arm 5 run slot

  base := runIdx * NVC
  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  if shape == SH_PS
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: stream's first long right in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 records (. right, X wrong); first wrong value "))
    ln_h(runOtherVal[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  elseif shape == SH_R
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" sentinel "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SENT])
    ln_s(string(" other-offset "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_LANE])
    ln_s(string(" seed "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" stream "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | rep0 primer "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | rep0 not sentinel by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  elseif shape == SH_P
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" sentinel "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SENT])
    ln_s(string(" seed "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" stream "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | rep0 primer "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps (value or ptra) "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_ptr_dist(runIdx - RUN_FP)
    ln_out()
  elseif shape == SH_F
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: R "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_REL])
    ln_s(string(" S "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_OK])
    ln_s(string(" W "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_REL_WF])
    ln_s(string(" Q "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_OK_RF])
    ln_s(string(" V "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_OK_WF])
    ln_s(string(" L "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_LANE])
    ln_s(string(" D "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" F "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" X "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + FL_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | rep0 released value "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + FL_REL] + runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + FL_REL_WF])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" flags: preset C=1 Z=1 survived in "))
    ln_d(runNoFlag[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" records; after-settle flags differ from the immediate flags in "))
    ln_d(runLate[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" records; first unpredicted flags long (bit0 C bit1 Z immediate, bit2 C bit3 Z late) "))
    if runFlagVal[runIdx] == -1
      ln_s(string("none"))
    else
      ln_hx(runFlagVal[runIdx], 1)
    ln_out()
  elseif shape == SH_W
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps, values (rb1+rb2): old "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OLD])
    ln_s(string(" new "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_NEW])
    ln_s(string(" primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" seed "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" other-lane "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_LANE])
    ln_s(string(" stream "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of 2048; (new,new) cells "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" rep0 cells: OO "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_OO])
    ln_s(string(" PN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_PN])
    ln_s(string(" NN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_NN])
    ln_s(string(" ON "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_ON])
    ln_s(string(" DN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_DN])
    ln_s(string(" any other pair "))
    ln_d(NCELL - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_OO] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_PN] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_NN] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_ON] - runRep0[runIdx * NPAIR + PAIR_DN])
    ln_s(string(" | OO by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | not NN by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_out()
  else
    bIdx := runIdx - RUN_Q
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps (records of 8 longs): right block "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_OK])
    ln_s(string(" primer-in-record "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" seed-in-record "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" both "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_MIX])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" unwritten "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_UNWR])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | rep0 records with the primer by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | rep0 not the right block by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" per long 0-7, all reps: primer "))
    ln_row8(@blkPrim[bIdx * BLKN])
    ln_s(string(" | seed "))
    ln_row8(@blkSeed[bIdx * BLKN])
    ln_s(string(" | other "))
    ln_row8(@blkOth[bIdx * BLKN])
    if blkOthIdx[bIdx] <> -1
      ln_s(string(" | first other value "))
      ln_h(blkOthVal[bIdx])
      ln_s(string(" in long "))
      ln_d(blkOthIdx[bIdx])
    ln_out()
  if shape <> SH_PS and shape <> SH_B
    if runOther[runIdx] > 0
      ln_lead(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" first other value "))
      ln_h(runOtherVal[runIdx])
      ln_s(string(" ("))
      ln_d(runOther[runIdx])
      say(string(" other values in the run)"))
    if runCnt[base + VC_STRM] > 0
      ln_lead(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" stream longs (F, data at a FIFO address): "))
      ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_STRM])
      ln_s(string(" values, first "))
      ln_h(runStrmVal[runIdx])
      ln_out()
    if (shape == SH_R or shape == SH_W or shape == SH_F) and runCnt[base + VC_LANE] > 0
      ln_lead(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" other-offset/other-lane values (L): "))
      ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_LANE])
      ln_s(string(", first "))
      ln_h(runLaneVal[runIdx])
      ln_out()
  if runCnt[base + VC_UNWR] > 0
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" never written (U, $EEEE_EEEE): "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_UNWR])
    say(string(" records"))

PRI ln_ptr_dist(pIdx) | grp
' Append a PTRA++ run's delta distribution, all repetitions, per value group.
'
' @param pIdx - PTRA++ run slot 0..2 (N, C, T)

' Local Variables:
' @local grp - value group: 0 released (primer), 1 correct (sentinel), 2 other

  ln_s(string(" ptra after minus before, all reps:"))
  repeat grp from 0 to 2
    ln_s(lookupz(grp: string(" released cells"), string(" | correct cells"), string(" | other values")))
    ln_s(string(": 0 x"))
    ln_d(ptrDel[pIdx * 9 + grp * 3])
    ln_s(string(", +4 x"))
    ln_d(ptrDel[pIdx * 9 + grp * 3 + 1])
    ln_s(string(", other x"))
    ln_d(ptrDel[pIdx * 9 + grp * 3 + 2])
  ln_s(string(" | first other delta "))
  ln_d(ptrOddDel[pIdx])

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' gates
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_gatefail(armIdx)
' Append the lead of a gate-failure line.
'
' @param armIdx - arm

  if armIdx == ARM_P
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): "))
  else
    ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm "))
    ln_d(armIdx)
    ln_s(string("): "))

PRI is_clean(runIdx) : bClean
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns bClean - every trial clean (R/F sentinel, PS right, W (new,new), B right block)

  bClean := runGoodAll[runIdx] == NTRIAL

PRI arm_gate(armIdx) : bPass | runIdx, kind, unwrCnt, otherCnt, disCnt
' Check the arm's gates; print a line for each that fails, and the result.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns bPass - TRUE when every gate of the arm passed

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run index
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local unwrCnt - never-written records over the arm
' @local otherCnt - X values in the gated control runs
' @local disCnt - disagreeing cells in the gated runs

  bPass := TRUE
  unwrCnt := 0
  otherCnt := 0
  disCnt := 0
  repeat runIdx from arm_first(armIdx) to arm_last(armIdx)
    kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
    unwrCnt += runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_UNWR]
    if kind == KD_NOP or kind == KD_PS
      if not is_clean(runIdx)
        ln_gatefail(armIdx)
        ln_runname(runIdx)
        ln_s(string(" (control) clean in "))
        ln_d(runGoodAll[runIdx])
        say(string(" of 1024 trials: the table, the addresses, the read or write path is wrong"))
        bPass := FALSE
      otherCnt += runOther[runIdx]
      disCnt += runDisagree[runIdx]
    elseif kind == KD_WAIT
      if armIdx <= ARM_WR
        otherCnt += runOther[runIdx]
      disCnt += runDisagree[runIdx]
    elseif armIdx <= ARM_WR and run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) <> SH_P
      ' a test run of arms 0-3 (the PTRA++ test run records, so it is not gated)
      disCnt += runDisagree[runIdx]
      armTestDis[armIdx] += runDisagree[runIdx]
  if unwrCnt > 0
    ln_gatefail(armIdx)
    ln_d(unwrCnt)
    say(string(" records still hold the fill $EEEE_EEEE: the measuring cog never wrote them"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if otherCnt > 0
    ln_gatefail(armIdx)
    ln_d(otherCnt)
    say(string(" values classified X (other) in a gated control run - see each run's 'first other value' line"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if disCnt > 0
    ln_gatefail(armIdx)
    ln_d(disCnt)
    say(string(" cells whose 16 repetitions disagree in a gated run: the result was not repeatable"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if armIdx == ARM_P
    if runRep0[RUN_T1 * NPAIR + VC_PRIM] <> T1_PRED or not delta_match(RUN_T1) or runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM] <> T1_PRED * REPS or runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_SENT] <> T1_PRED_SENT * REPS
      ln_gatefail(armIdx)
      ln_s(string("T1 k=0 did not reproduce Erratum E7: rep0 primer "))
      ln_d(runRep0[RUN_T1 * NPAIR + VC_PRIM])
      ln_s(string(" (MUST 43) by delta "))
      ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_T1 * NSLOT])
      ln_s(string(" (MUST 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2); all reps primer "))
      ln_d(runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM])
      ln_s(string(" (MUST 688) sentinel "))
      ln_d(runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_SENT])
      say(string(" (MUST 336)"))
      bPass := FALSE
    if not is_clean(RUN_T1F)
      ln_gatefail(armIdx)
      ln_s(string("T1 k=7 sentinel in "))
      ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_T1F])
      say(string(" of 1024 records (MUST 1024, no release from k=7)"))
      bPass := FALSE
  if armIdx == ARM_Q and not baseOk
    ln_gatefail(armIdx)
    say(string("the baseline cog-RAM copy did not equal the loaded image: the integrity check cannot be read"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if armDamage[armIdx] > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE (arm "))
    ln_d(armIdx)
    ln_s(string("): "))
    ln_d(armDamage[armIdx])
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the arm (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))
  if armIdx <> ARM_P and bPass
    ln_s(string("GATES PASS (arm "))
    ln_d(armIdx)
    say(string("): every NOP control clean, no record left unwritten, no other value and no disagreeing repetitions in a gated run"))

PRI delta_match(runIdx) : bMatch | deltaIdx
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns bMatch - TRUE when the run's repetition-0 delta split is 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2

' Local Variables:
' @local deltaIdx - delta 0..7

  bMatch := TRUE
  repeat deltaIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + deltaIdx] <> predK0[deltaIdx]
      bMatch := FALSE

PRI is_rel_code(runIdx, code) : bRel | shape
' @param runIdx - run index
' @param code - a repetition-0 cell code
' @returns bRel - TRUE when the cell counts as released (R: primer, F: primer
'   value, W: (old,old), B: primer in the record)

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  if shape == SH_W
    bRel := code == PAIR_OO
  elseif shape == SH_F
    bRel := code == FL_REL or code == FL_REL_WF
  elseif shape == SH_B
    bRel := code == BC_PRIM or code == BC_MIX
  else
    bRel := code == VC_PRIM

PRI map_match(runIdx) : matchCnt | cellIdx
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns matchCnt - cells whose released / not-released status equals T1 k=0's

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar

  matchCnt := 0
  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    if is_rel_code(runIdx, cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]) == (cellCode[RUN_T1 * NCELL + cellIdx] == VC_PRIM)
      matchCnt++

PRI rel_cells(runIdx) : relCnt | cellIdx
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns relCnt - repetition-0 cells counted as released

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar

  relCnt := 0
  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    if is_rel_code(runIdx, cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx])
      relCnt++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' verdicts
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_arm_verdicts(armIdx, bDetail)
' @param armIdx - arm
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

  if armIdx == ARM_P
    print_rig_line()
  elseif armIdx == ARM_FL
    verdict_flags(FALSE, bDetail)
    verdict_flags(TRUE, bDetail)
    observed_ptr()
  elseif armIdx == ARM_RD
    verdict_rd(FALSE, bDetail)
    verdict_rd(TRUE, bDetail)
  elseif armIdx == ARM_WR
    verdict_wr(FALSE, bDetail)
    verdict_wr(TRUE, bDetail)
  elseif armIdx == ARM_WF
    observed_wf_r(bDetail)
    observed_wf_w(bDetail)
  else
    observed_q(bDetail)

PRI print_summary() | armIdx
' Repeat every arm's verdict line, so the closing block holds them all.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm

  say(string("=== VERDICT SUMMARY (each arm's verdict as printed at its end; arms not completed say so) ==="))
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARM - 1
    print_arm_verdicts(armIdx, FALSE)

PRI ln_notdone(armIdx) : bNotDone
' If the arm did not complete, append the reason to the line, send it, and
' return TRUE.  The caller has already appended the verdict's name.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns bNotDone - TRUE when the arm did not complete (line sent)

  bNotDone := not armDone[armIdx]
  if bNotDone
    ln_s(string("NOT COMPLETED - the run ended before arm "))
    ln_d(armIdx)
    say(string(" finished (see the RIG FAIL line above)"))

PRI ln_nogate(armIdx) : bNoGate
' If arm 0 or this arm's gate failed, append NO VERDICT, send, return TRUE.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns bNoGate - TRUE when no verdict may be given (line sent)

  bNoGate := not armPass[ARM_P] or not armPass[armIdx]
  if bNoGate
    if not armPass[ARM_P]
      say(string("NO VERDICT - arm 0 (positive control) failed: no later verdict counts; the rows above are raw"))
    else
      ln_s(string("NO VERDICT - a gate of arm "))
      ln_d(armIdx)
      ln_s(string(" failed (see GATE FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
      if armTestDis[armIdx] > 0
        ln_s(string("; disagreeing repetitions in a test run may be a result: see the rows ("))
        ln_d(armTestDis[armIdx])
        ln_s(string(" cells)"))
      ln_out()

PRI print_rig_line()
' Arm 0's verdict: RIG OK or RIG FAIL.
'

  if not armDone[ARM_P]
    say(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): arm 0 did not complete (see the RIG FAIL line above)"))
  elseif armPass[ARM_P]
    ln_s(string("RIG OK (arm 0, positive control): Erratum E7 reproduced - C1 sentinel and PS stream long in all 1024 records, T1 k=0 43 primer per repetition by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 "))
    say(string("(688 primer, 336 sentinel), T1 k=7 sentinel in all 1024, no U, no X, every cell's 16 repetitions identical"))
  else
    say(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): Erratum E7 not reproduced (see the lines above) - no later verdict counts"))

PRI verdict_flags(bZ, bDetail)
' VERDICT E7 FLAGS C (FC) / FLAGS Z (FZ).
'
' @param bZ - FALSE: FC (C decides); TRUE: FZ (Z decides)
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

  if bZ
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 FLAGS Z: "))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 FLAGS C: "))
  if not ln_notdone(ARM_FL)
    if not ln_nogate(ARM_FL)
      verdict_flags_body(bZ, bDetail)

PRI verdict_flags_body(bZ, bDetail) | varIdx, rWait, rT, relCnt, mapCnt, relWf, okRf, okWf, oddCnt
' The FLAGS C / FLAGS Z verdict once the arm's gates have passed.
'
' @param bZ - FALSE: FC (C decides); TRUE: FZ (Z decides)
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

' Local Variables:
' @local varIdx - variant 0 (FC) or 1 (FZ)
' @local rWait - waiting-form run
' @local rT - test run
' @local relCnt - repetition-0 cells holding the released value
' @local mapCnt - cells whose status equals T1's
' @local relWf - records: primer value, wrong flags
' @local okRf - records: sentinel with the released flags
' @local okWf - records: sentinel with other flags
' @local oddCnt - records neither primer nor sentinel value (seed, stream, other)

  varIdx := bZ & 1
  rWait := RUN_FL + varIdx * 3 + 1
  rT := rWait + 1
  set_ref(rT)
  relCnt := rel_cells(rT)
  mapCnt := map_match(rT)
  relWf := runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_REL_WF]
  okRf := runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_OK_RF]
  okWf := runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_OK_WF]
  oddCnt := runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_SEED] + runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_STRM] + runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_OTHER]
  if not is_clean(rWait)
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - the waiting-form control was (sentinel, C=0, Z=0) in only "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[rWait])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 records"))
  elseif relWf + okRf + okWf > 0
    if runNoFlag[rT] > 0
      ln_s(string("REFUTED - flags not written by the released read: the preset C=1 Z=1 survived in "))
      ln_d(runNoFlag[rT])
      ln_s(string(" records"))
    else
      ln_s(string("REFUTED - a read's flags are not its value's"))
    ln_s(string("; released value with other flags "))
    ln_d(relWf)
    ln_s(string(", sentinel with released flags "))
    ln_d(okRf)
    ln_s(string(", sentinel with other flags "))
    ln_d(okWf)
    ln_s(string(" (first flags long "))
    ln_hx(runFlagVal[rT], 1)
    ln_c(")")
  elseif oddCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - "))
    ln_d(oddCnt)
    ln_s(string(" records are neither the released value nor the sentinel (seed, stream, other): the value side departs from Erratum E7"))
  elseif relCnt == 0
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - no cell released in this run, so a released RDLONG's flags were not seen"))
  elseif relCnt == T1_PRED and mapCnt == NCELL and runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_REL] == T1_PRED * REPS
    if runLate[rT] > 0
      ln_s(string("CONFIRMED AT THE READ, BUT FLAGS CHANGED AFTER THE READ in "))
      ln_d(runLate[rT])
      ln_s(string(" records - right after the read every record had its value's flags; released in T1's same 43 cells"))
    else
      ln_s(string("CONFIRMED - every released record carried the predicted flags and every correct record its own; released in T1's same 43 cells in every repetition"))
  else
    ln_s(string("MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - every record's flags as predicted, but the released cells are not T1's 43"))
    if runLate[rT] > 0
      ln_s(string("; flags changed after the read in "))
      ln_d(runLate[rT])
      ln_s(string(" records"))
  ln_s(string(" | before the run: released ("))
  ln_h(refPrim)
  ln_s(string(", "))
  ln_flags(refRelFl)
  ln_s(string(") / correct ("))
  ln_h(refSent)
  ln_s(string(", "))
  ln_flags(refOkFl)
  ln_s(string(") | released cells "))
  ln_d(relCnt)
  ln_s(string(" per repetition (T1: 43), same cells as T1 in "))
  ln_d(mapCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of 64; late flag changes "))
  ln_d(runLate[rT])
  ln_out()
  if bDetail
    ln_s(string("  detail: by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[rT * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" (T1: 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2); records R "))
    ln_d(runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_REL])
    ln_s(string(" S "))
    ln_d(runCnt[rT * NVC + FL_OK])
    ln_s(string(" W "))
    ln_d(relWf)
    ln_s(string(" Q "))
    ln_d(okRf)
    ln_s(string(" V "))
    ln_d(okWf)
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(oddCnt)
    ln_s(string(" of 1024; preset flags survived in "))
    ln_d(runNoFlag[rT])
    say(string(" records"))

PRI observed_ptr() | rT
' OBSERVED E7 PTRA++ (records): the PTRA delta of rdlong dst,ptra++ at
' k=0, split by released / correct cells.  Gated on arm 0 and arm 1 (whose
' gate includes the PTRA++ NOP control and waiting form, not its test run).
'

' Local Variables:
' @local rT - the PTRA++ test run

  rT := RUN_FP + 2
  ln_s(string("OBSERVED E7 PTRA++: "))
  if not ln_notdone(ARM_FL)
    if not ln_nogate(ARM_FL)
      ln_s(string("released cells (rep0) "))
      ln_d(runRep0[rT * NPAIR + VC_PRIM])
      ln_s(string(" of 64 (same cells as T1: "))
      ln_d(map_match(rT))
      ln_s(string(" of 64);"))
      ln_ptr_dist(rT - RUN_FP)
      ln_s(string(" | waiting form (sentinel, +4) "))
      ln_d(runGoodAll[rT - 1])
      ln_s(string(" of 1024; disagreeing cells "))
      ln_d(runDisagree[rT])
      ln_out()

PRI ln_rd_values(bWord) | varIdx
' Append the byte/word values written before the run (released / not released).
'
' @param bWord - FALSE: the byte instruction; TRUE: the word instruction

' Local Variables:
' @local varIdx - variant

  ln_s(string(" | before the run (value,C,Z), released (prediction A): "))
  repeat varIdx from 0 to NVAR - 1
    if (varIdx >= 4) == bWord
      ln_rd_triple(varIdx, PRIMB)
  ln_s(string("; not released (sentinel part): "))
  repeat varIdx from 0 to NVAR - 1
    if (varIdx >= 4) == bWord
      ln_rd_triple(varIdx, SENTB)

PRI ln_rd_triple(varIdx, longVal) | partVal
' Append "off<n> $<part> C<c>Z<z> " for one arm 2 variant.
'
' @param varIdx - arm 2/3 variant 0..5
' @param longVal - the long

' Local Variables:
' @local partVal - the part read at the variant's offset

  partVal := part(longVal, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx))
  ln_s(string("off"))
  ln_d(var_lane(varIdx))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_hx(partVal, var_size(varIdx) * 2)
  ln_s(string(" C"))
  ln_d(flags_of(partVal, var_size(varIdx)) & 1)
  ln_c("Z")
  ln_d((flags_of(partVal, var_size(varIdx)) >> 1) & 1)
  ln_c(" ")

PRI verdict_rd(bWord, bDetail)
' VERDICT E7 RDBYTE / RDWORD, in the order fixed in the header.
'
' @param bWord - FALSE: the byte instruction; TRUE: the word instruction
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

  if bWord
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDWORD: "))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 RDBYTE: "))
  if not ln_notdone(ARM_RD)
    if not ln_nogate(ARM_RD)
      verdict_rd_body(bWord, bDetail)

PRI verdict_rd_body(bWord, bDetail) | varIdx, vFirst, vLast, rNop, rWait, rNear, rFar, badC, seedCnt, laneCnt, laneVal, laneRun, othCnt, othVal, othRun, relNear, relFar, bAll, flWrong, flPreset, flLate
' The RDBYTE / RDWORD verdict once the arm's gates have passed.
'
' @param bWord - FALSE: the byte instruction; TRUE: the word instruction
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

' Local Variables:
' @local varIdx - variant
' @local vFirst - first variant of the instruction
' @local vLast - last variant
' @local rNop - NOP control run
' @local rWait - waiting-form run
' @local rNear - test k=0 run
' @local rFar - test k=7 run
' @local badC - waiting-form runs not clean
' @local seedCnt - seed records in the test runs
' @local laneCnt - other-offset records in the test runs
' @local laneVal - the first such value
' @local laneRun - its run
' @local othCnt - other or stream records in the test runs
' @local othVal - the first such value
' @local othRun - its run
' @local relNear - repetition-0 released cells at k=0, summed over the offsets
' @local relFar - the same at k=7
' @local bAll - every offset exactly as predicted
' @local flWrong - k=0 records whose flags are not their value's
' @local flPreset - k=0 records whose preset flags C=1 Z=1 survived
' @local flLate - k=0 records whose flags changed after the read

  if bWord
    vFirst := 4
    vLast := 5
  else
    vFirst := 0
    vLast := 3
  badC := 0
  seedCnt := 0
  laneCnt := 0
  othCnt := 0
  laneRun := -1
  othRun := -1
  relNear := 0
  relFar := 0
  bAll := TRUE
  flWrong := 0
  flPreset := 0
  flLate := 0
  repeat varIdx from vFirst to vLast
    rNop := RUN_RD + varIdx * 4
    rWait := rNop + SL_C
    rNear := rNop + SL_T0               ' value + flags run (FL_* classes)
    rFar := rNop + SL_T7                ' image R run (VC_* classes)
    if not is_clean(rWait)
      badC++
    seedCnt += runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_SEED] + runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_SEED]
    flWrong += runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_REL_WF] + runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_OK_RF] + runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_OK_WF]
    flPreset += runNoFlag[rNear]
    flLate += runLate[rNear]
    if laneRun == -1 and runCnt[rNear * NVC + VC_LANE] > 0
      laneRun := rNear
      laneVal := runLaneVal[rNear]
    if laneRun == -1 and runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_LANE] > 0
      laneRun := rFar
      laneVal := runLaneVal[rFar]
    laneCnt += runCnt[rNear * NVC + VC_LANE] + runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_LANE]
    if othRun == -1 and runCnt[rNear * NVC + VC_OTHER] > 0
      othRun := rNear
      othVal := runOtherVal[rNear]
    if othRun == -1 and runCnt[rNear * NVC + VC_STRM] > 0
      othRun := rNear
      othVal := runStrmVal[rNear]
    if othRun == -1 and runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_OTHER] > 0
      othRun := rFar
      othVal := runOtherVal[rFar]
    if othRun == -1 and runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_STRM] > 0
      othRun := rFar
      othVal := runStrmVal[rFar]
    othCnt += runCnt[rNear * NVC + VC_OTHER] + runCnt[rNear * NVC + VC_STRM] + runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_OTHER] + runCnt[rFar * NVC + VC_STRM]
    relNear += rel_cells(rNear)
    relFar += runRep0[rFar * NPAIR + VC_PRIM]
    if rel_cells(rNear) <> T1_PRED or map_match(rNear) <> NCELL or not delta_match(rNear) or runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_REL] + runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_REL_WF] <> T1_PRED * REPS or not is_clean(rFar)
      bAll := FALSE
  if badC > 0
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - "))
    ln_d(badC)
    ln_s(string(" waiting-form control(s) at k=0 not (sentinel part, its flags) in every record"))
  elseif seedCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - a released read did not write its destination: "))
    ln_d(seedCnt)
    ln_s(string(" seed records in the test runs"))
  elseif laneCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - prediction A's shift is wrong: "))
    ln_d(laneCnt)
    ln_s(string(" records hold the primer's part at another offset (first "))
    ln_h(laneVal)
    ln_s(string(" in "))
    ln_runname(laneRun)
    ln_c(")")
  elseif othCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - a released value is not the previous read's: "))
    ln_d(othCnt)
    ln_s(string(" other or stream records (first "))
    ln_h(othVal)
    ln_s(string(" in "))
    ln_runname(othRun)
    ln_c(")")
  elseif relNear == 0 and relFar == 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - no early release: every test record the sentinel part at k=0 and k=7"))
  elseif flWrong > 0
    if flPreset > 0
      ln_s(string("REFUTED - flags not written by the released read (preset C=1 Z=1 survived in "))
      ln_d(flPreset)
      ln_s(string(" records); values as prediction A"))
    else
      ln_s(string("REFUTED - values as prediction A, but flags are not the value's in "))
      ln_d(flWrong)
      ln_s(string(" k=0 records"))
  elseif bAll and flLate > 0
    ln_s(string("CONFIRMED AT THE READ, BUT FLAGS CHANGED AFTER THE READ in "))
    ln_d(flLate)
    ln_s(string(" records - prediction A with its flags in T1's 43 cells at every offset; k=7 none"))
  elseif bAll
    ln_s(string("CONFIRMED - at every offset prediction A with its flags in T1's same 43 cells in every repetition, the rest the sentinel part with its flags; k=7 none"))
  else
    ln_s(string("MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - values and flags as predicted, but released cells k=0 "))
    ln_d(relNear)
    ln_s(string(" / k=7 "))
    ln_d(relFar)
    ln_s(string(" over the offsets (predicted 43 per offset / 0)"))
  ln_s(string(" | flags at k=0: not the value's "))
  ln_d(flWrong)
  ln_s(string(", preset survived "))
  ln_d(flPreset)
  ln_s(string(", changed after the read "))
  ln_d(flLate)
  ln_rd_values(bWord)
  ln_out()
  if bDetail
    repeat varIdx from vFirst to vLast
      rNop := RUN_RD + varIdx * 4
      ln_s(string("  detail offset "))
      ln_d(var_lane(varIdx))
      ln_s(string(": k=0 released "))
      ln_d(rel_cells(rNop + SL_T0))
      ln_s(string(" of 64 (same cells as T1: "))
      ln_d(map_match(rNop + SL_T0))
      ln_s(string(" of 64) by delta "))
      ln_row8(@runDelta[(rNop + SL_T0) * NSLOT])
      ln_s(string("; k=0 records R/S/W/Q/V "))
      ln_d(runCnt[(rNop + SL_T0) * NVC + FL_REL])
      ln_c("/")
      ln_d(runCnt[(rNop + SL_T0) * NVC + FL_OK])
      ln_c("/")
      ln_d(runCnt[(rNop + SL_T0) * NVC + FL_REL_WF])
      ln_c("/")
      ln_d(runCnt[(rNop + SL_T0) * NVC + FL_OK_RF])
      ln_c("/")
      ln_d(runCnt[(rNop + SL_T0) * NVC + FL_OK_WF])
      ln_s(string(" | k=7 released "))
      ln_d(runRep0[(rNop + SL_T7) * NPAIR + VC_PRIM])
      ln_s(string(" | waiting k=0 (sentinel part, flags) "))
      ln_d(runGoodAll[rNop + SL_C])
      ln_s(string(" of 1024 | NOP control "))
      ln_d(runGoodAll[rNop + SL_N])
      say(string(" of 1024"))

PRI ln_wr_values(bWord) | varIdx
' Append the write values written before the run.
'
' @param bWord - FALSE: the byte instruction; TRUE: the word instruction

' Local Variables:
' @local varIdx - variant

  ln_s(string(" | before the run: released = write lost, target stays $4C3D_2E1F (old,old), or read-back released (primer $A5A5_0001, new); not released = (new,new), new "))
  repeat varIdx from 0 to NVAR - 1
    if (varIdx >= 4) == bWord
      ln_s(string("off"))
      ln_d(var_lane(varIdx))
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_h(merge(OLDB, NEWD, var_size(varIdx), var_lane(varIdx)))
      ln_c(" ")

PRI verdict_wr(bWord, bDetail)
' VERDICT E7 WRBYTE / WRWORD, in the order fixed in the header.
'
' @param bWord - FALSE: the byte instruction; TRUE: the word instruction
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

  if bWord
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRWORD: "))
  else
    ln_s(string("VERDICT E7 WRBYTE: "))
  if not ln_notdone(ARM_WR)
    if not ln_nogate(ARM_WR)
      verdict_wr_body(bWord, bDetail)

PRI verdict_wr_body(bWord, bDetail) | varIdx, vFirst, vLast, rNop, rWait, rW1, rW2, badC, cntON, old2, allNN, unnamed, oo, pn, nn, sumOO, bAll, c1Idx
' The WRBYTE / WRWORD verdict once the arm's gates have passed.
'
' @param bWord - FALSE: the byte instruction; TRUE: the word instruction
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

' Local Variables:
' @local varIdx - variant
' @local vFirst - first variant of the instruction
' @local vLast - last variant
' @local rNop - NOP control run
' @local rWait - waiting-form run
' @local rW1 - test W1 run
' @local rW2 - test W2 run
' @local badC - waiting-form runs not clean
' @local cntON - W1 cells (old,new) over the offsets
' @local old2 - W2 cells with rb2 old over the offsets
' @local allNN - offsets whose W1 is (new,new) in all 64 and W2 (seed,new) in all 64
' @local unnamed - offsets with a W1 cell outside OO/PN/NN or a W2 cell not (seed,new)
' @local oo - W1 (old,old) cells at this offset
' @local pn - W1 (primer,new) cells at this offset
' @local nn - W1 (new,new) cells at this offset
' @local sumOO - W1 (old,old) cells over the offsets
' @local bAll - every offset exactly as predicted
' @local c1Idx - rb1 class

  if bWord
    vFirst := 4
    vLast := 5
  else
    vFirst := 0
    vLast := 3
  badC := 0
  cntON := 0
  old2 := 0
  allNN := 0
  unnamed := 0
  sumOO := 0
  bAll := TRUE
  repeat varIdx from vFirst to vLast
    rNop := RUN_WR + varIdx * 4
    rWait := rNop + SW_C
    rW1 := rNop + SW_T1
    rW2 := rNop + SW_T2
    if not is_clean(rWait)
      badC++
    oo := runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_OO]
    pn := runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_PN]
    nn := runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_NN]
    sumOO += oo
    cntON += runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_ON]
    repeat c1Idx from 0 to NVC - 1
      old2 += runRep0[rW2 * NPAIR + c1Idx * NVC + VC_OLD]
    if nn == NCELL and runRep0[rW2 * NPAIR + PAIR_DN] == NCELL
      allNN++
    if oo + pn + nn <> NCELL or runRep0[rW2 * NPAIR + PAIR_DN] <> NCELL
      unnamed++
    if oo <> T3_PRED_OO or pn <> T3_PRED_PN or not delta_match(rW1) or map_match(rW1) <> NCELL or runRep0[rW2 * NPAIR + PAIR_DN] <> NCELL
      bAll := FALSE
  if badC > 0
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - "))
    ln_d(badC)
    ln_s(string(" waiting-form control(s) not (new,new) in every cell"))
  elseif cntON > 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - writes land after all (W1: old,new): "))
    ln_d(cntON)
    ln_s(string(" cells; W2 cells with rb2 old "))
    ln_d(old2)
  elseif old2 > 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - released write never lands (W2: rb2 old): "))
    ln_d(old2)
    ln_s(string(" cells"))
  elseif allNN == vLast - vFirst + 1
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - defect absent: W1 (new,new) in all 64 cells and W2 (seed,new) in all 64, at every offset"))
  elseif unnamed > 0 or sumOO == 0
    ln_s(string("REFUTED - a pattern the prediction does not name (another lane written, other values, or no lost write) at "))
    ln_d(unnamed)
    ln_s(string(" offset(s); W1 (old,old) cells over the offsets "))
    ln_d(sumOO)
  elseif bAll
    ln_s(string("CONFIRMED - at every offset W1 43 (old,old) in T1's cells (the write lost, the target's old long unchanged) + 21 (primer,new), W2 (seed,new) in all 64"))
  else
    ln_s(string("MECHANISM PRESENT, COUNT DIFFERS - lost writes present, but not 43 (old,old) + 21 (primer,new) in T1's cells at every offset; W1 (old,old) over the offsets "))
    ln_d(sumOO)
  ln_wr_values(bWord)
  ln_out()
  if bDetail
    repeat varIdx from vFirst to vLast
      rNop := RUN_WR + varIdx * 4
      rW1 := rNop + SW_T1
      ln_s(string("  detail offset "))
      ln_d(var_lane(varIdx))
      ln_s(string(": W1 OO "))
      ln_d(runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_OO])
      ln_s(string(" PN "))
      ln_d(runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_PN])
      ln_s(string(" NN "))
      ln_d(runRep0[rW1 * NPAIR + PAIR_NN])
      ln_s(string(" (same cells as T1: "))
      ln_d(map_match(rW1))
      ln_s(string(" of 64) OO by delta "))
      ln_row8(@runDelta[rW1 * NSLOT])
      ln_s(string(" | W2 (seed,new) "))
      ln_d(runRep0[(rNop + SW_T2) * NPAIR + PAIR_DN])
      ln_s(string(" | waiting (new,new) "))
      ln_d(runGoodAll[rNop + SW_C])
      ln_s(string(" of 1024 | NOP control (new,new) "))
      ln_d(runGoodAll[rNop + SW_N])
      say(string(" of 1024"))

PRI observed_wf_r(bDetail)
' OBSERVED E7 WRFAST-RDLONG (records).
'
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

  ln_s(string("OBSERVED E7 WRFAST-RDLONG: "))
  if not ln_wfhang()
    if not ln_notdone(ARM_WF)
      if not ln_nogate(ARM_WF)
        observed_wf_r_body(bDetail)

PRI observed_wf_r_body(bDetail) | rWait, rNear, rFar, primNear, primFar, primWait, oddCnt, flWrong, flPreset, flLate, rIdx
' The WRFAST-RDLONG record once the arm's gates have passed.
'
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

' Local Variables:
' @local rWait - waiting WRFAST run
' @local rNear - no-wait WRFAST k=0 run
' @local rFar - no-wait WRFAST k=7 run
' @local primNear - repetition-0 primer cells at k=0
' @local primFar - the same at k=7
' @local primWait - the same in the waiting form
' @local oddCnt - records neither primer nor sentinel in the three runs
' @local flWrong - records whose flags are not their value's, three runs
' @local flPreset - records whose preset flags survived, three runs
' @local flLate - records whose flags changed after the read, three runs
' @local rIdx - run index

  rWait := RUN_WF + 1
  rNear := RUN_WF + 2
  rFar := RUN_WF + 3
  ' value + flags runs: released value = FL_REL or FL_REL_WF
  primNear := rel_cells(rNear)
  primFar := rel_cells(rFar)
  primWait := rel_cells(rWait)
  oddCnt := NTRIAL * 3 - wf_valued(rNear) - wf_valued(rFar) - wf_valued(rWait)
  flWrong := 0
  flPreset := 0
  flLate := 0
  repeat rIdx from rWait to rFar
    flWrong += runCnt[rIdx * NVC + FL_REL_WF] + runCnt[rIdx * NVC + FL_OK_RF] + runCnt[rIdx * NVC + FL_OK_WF]
    flPreset += runNoFlag[rIdx]
    flLate += runLate[rIdx]
  if primNear + primFar + primWait == 0
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: no early release - no primer record after the no-wait WRFAST at k=0 or k=7, nor after the waiting WRFAST"))
  else
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: released early in "))
    ln_d(primNear)
    ln_s(string(" of 64 cells at k=0 (rep0 primer cells; same cells as T1 in "))
    ln_d(map_match(rNear))
    ln_s(string(" of 64), "))
    ln_d(primFar)
    ln_s(string(" at k=7, "))
    ln_d(primWait)
    ln_s(string(" after the waiting WRFAST"))
  ln_s(string("; records neither primer nor sentinel (seed, stream, other) "))
  ln_d(oddCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of 3072; flags not the value's "))
  ln_d(flWrong)
  ln_s(string(", preset C=1 Z=1 survived "))
  ln_d(flPreset)
  ln_s(string(", changed after the read "))
  ln_d(flLate)
  ln_s(string("; cells with disagreeing reps "))
  ln_d(runDisagree[rNear] + runDisagree[rFar] + runDisagree[rWait])
  ln_out()
  if bDetail
    ln_s(string("  detail: k=0 primer by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[rNear * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(", not (sentinel, C=0 Z=0) by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[rNear * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | k=7 primer by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[rFar * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | waiting (sentinel, C=0 Z=0) "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[rWait])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | seed k=0/k=7/waiting "))
    ln_d(runCnt[rNear * NVC + FL_SEED])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runCnt[rFar * NVC + FL_SEED])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runCnt[rWait * NVC + FL_SEED])
    say(string(" (per-run class counts in each run's totals lines)"))

PRI wf_valued(runIdx) : cnt
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns cnt - records whose value is the primer or the sentinel (any flags)

  cnt := runCnt[runIdx * NVC + FL_REL] + runCnt[runIdx * NVC + FL_REL_WF] + runCnt[runIdx * NVC + FL_OK] + runCnt[runIdx * NVC + FL_OK_RF] + runCnt[runIdx * NVC + FL_OK_WF]

PRI ln_wfhang() : bHang
' If an arm 4 command timed out, append the hang report, send it, return TRUE.
' The caller has already appended the verdict's name.
'
' @returns bHang - TRUE when arm 4 stopped on a timeout (line sent)

  bHang := wfHang
  if bHang
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: blocking rdfast #0 after a no-wait WRFAST did not complete (run "))
    ln_runname(wfHangRun)
    say(string("); arm 4 stopped there and its remaining runs were skipped; the runs before it are raw rows above"))

PRI observed_wf_w(bDetail)
' OBSERVED E7 WRFAST-WRLONG (records).
'
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

  ln_s(string("OBSERVED E7 WRFAST-WRLONG: "))
  if not ln_wfhang()
    if not ln_notdone(ARM_WF)
      if not ln_nogate(ARM_WF)
        observed_wf_w_body(bDetail)

PRI observed_wf_w_body(bDetail) | rWait, rNear, rFar, rSecond, notNewNear, notNewFar, notNewWait, oldSecond, seedNewSecond, oddPairs
' The WRFAST-WRLONG record once the arm's gates have passed.
'
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

' Local Variables:
' @local rWait - waiting WRFAST W1 run
' @local rNear - no-wait WRFAST W1 k=0 run
' @local rFar - no-wait WRFAST W1 k=7 run
' @local rSecond - no-wait WRFAST W2 k=0 run
' @local notNewNear - W1 k=0 rep0 cells not (new,new)
' @local notNewFar - W1 k=7 rep0 cells not (new,new)
' @local notNewWait - waiting rep0 cells not (new,new)
' @local oldSecond - W2 rep0 cells with rb2 old
' @local seedNewSecond - W2 rep0 cells (seed,new)
' @local oddPairs - W1 k=0 rep0 cells outside OO/PN/NN/ON

  rWait := RUN_WFW + 1
  rNear := RUN_WFW + 2
  rFar := RUN_WFW + 3
  rSecond := RUN_WFW + 4
  notNewNear := NCELL - runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_NN]
  notNewFar := NCELL - runRep0[rFar * NPAIR + PAIR_NN]
  notNewWait := NCELL - runRep0[rWait * NPAIR + PAIR_NN]
  seedNewSecond := runRep0[rSecond * NPAIR + PAIR_DN]
  oldSecond := 0
  repeat oddPairs from 0 to NVC - 1
    oldSecond += runRep0[rSecond * NPAIR + oddPairs * NVC + VC_OLD]
  oddPairs := notNewNear - runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_OO] - runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_PN] - runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_ON]
  if notNewNear + notNewFar + notNewWait == 0 and seedNewSecond == NCELL
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: no early release - W1 (new,new) in all 64 cells at k=0 and k=7 and after the waiting WRFAST; W2 (seed,new) in all 64"))
  else
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: released early in "))
    ln_d(notNewNear)
    ln_s(string(" of 64 cells at k=0 W1 (not (new,new): OO "))
    ln_d(runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_OO])
    ln_s(string(" PN "))
    ln_d(runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_PN])
    ln_s(string(" ON "))
    ln_d(runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + PAIR_ON])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(oddPairs)
    ln_s(string("), "))
    ln_d(notNewFar)
    ln_s(string(" at k=7, "))
    ln_d(notNewWait)
    ln_s(string(" after the waiting WRFAST; W2 k=0 (seed,new) "))
    ln_d(seedNewSecond)
    ln_s(string(", rb2 old "))
    ln_d(oldSecond)
  ln_s(string("; cells with disagreeing reps "))
  ln_d(runDisagree[rNear] + runDisagree[rFar] + runDisagree[rWait] + runDisagree[rSecond])
  ln_out()
  if bDetail
    ln_s(string("  detail: W1 k=0 OO by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[rNear * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(", not NN by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[rNear * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" (same OO cells as T1's primer cells: "))
    ln_d(map_match(rNear))
    ln_s(string(" of 64) | W1 k=7 not NN by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[rFar * NSLOT])
    say(string(" (per-run counts in each run's totals lines)"))

PRI observed_q(bDetail) | bIdx, intTot, intMissing
' OBSERVED E7 SETQ-BLOCK (records), with the cog-RAM integrity result.
'
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines

' Local Variables:
' @local bIdx - arm 5 run slot
' @local intTot - changed cog registers over the arm's runs
' @local intMissing - arm 5 runs whose cog-RAM copy never arrived

  ln_s(string("OBSERVED E7 SETQ-BLOCK: "))
  intTot := 0
  intMissing := 0
  repeat bIdx from 0 to NBRUN - 1
    if intChanged[bIdx] == -1
      intMissing++
    else
      intTot += intChanged[bIdx]
  if bLost
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: measuring cog lost during the SETQ block arm (run "))
    ln_runname(lostRun)
    ln_s(string("); cog-RAM registers changed outside the sacrificial range in the completed runs "))
    ln_d(intTot)
    say(string(" (see INTEGRITY lines)"))
  elseif not ln_notdone(ARM_Q)
    if not armPass[ARM_P] or not armPass[ARM_Q]
      ln_s(string("NO VERDICT - "))
      if not armPass[ARM_P]
        ln_s(string("arm 0 (positive control) failed"))
      else
        ln_s(string("a gate of arm 5 failed (see GATE FAIL lines)"))
      ln_s(string("; the rows above are raw; cog-RAM registers changed outside the sacrificial range "))
      ln_d(intTot)
      say(string(" (see INTEGRITY lines)"))
    else
      observed_q_body(bDetail, intTot, intMissing)

PRI observed_q_body(bDetail, intTot, intMissing) | rWait, rNear, rFar, primNear, primFar, primWait, oddCnt
' The SETQ-BLOCK record once the arm's gates have passed.
'
' @param bDetail - TRUE: add the detail lines
' @param intTot - changed cog registers over the arm's runs
' @param intMissing - arm 5 runs whose cog-RAM copy never arrived

' Local Variables:
' @local rWait - waiting-form run
' @local rNear - no-wait k=0 run
' @local rFar - no-wait k=7 run
' @local primNear - repetition-0 records with the primer at k=0
' @local primFar - the same at k=7
' @local primWait - the same in the waiting form
' @local oddCnt - records with seed or other longs and no primer, in the three runs

  rWait := RUN_Q + 1
  rNear := RUN_Q + 2
  rFar := RUN_Q + 3
  primNear := runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + BC_PRIM] + runRep0[rNear * NPAIR + BC_MIX]
  primFar := runRep0[rFar * NPAIR + BC_PRIM] + runRep0[rFar * NPAIR + BC_MIX]
  primWait := runRep0[rWait * NPAIR + BC_PRIM] + runRep0[rWait * NPAIR + BC_MIX]
  oddCnt := runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_SEED] + runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_OTHER] + runCnt[rFar * NVC + BC_SEED] + runCnt[rFar * NVC + BC_OTHER] + runCnt[rWait * NVC + BC_SEED] + runCnt[rWait * NVC + BC_OTHER]
  if primNear + primFar + primWait == 0
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: no early release - no record holds the primer at k=0, k=7 or in the waiting form"))
  else
    ln_s(string("OBSERVED: released early in "))
    ln_d(primNear)
    ln_s(string(" of 64 cells at k=0 (records with the primer in some long; same cells as T1 in "))
    ln_d(map_match(rNear))
    ln_s(string(" of 64), "))
    ln_d(primFar)
    ln_s(string(" at k=7, "))
    ln_d(primWait)
    ln_s(string(" in the waiting form"))
  ln_s(string("; records with seed or other longs and no primer "))
  ln_d(oddCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of 3072; cog-RAM registers changed outside the sacrificial range "))
  ln_d(intTot)
  if intMissing > 0
    ln_s(string(" (copies missing: "))
    ln_d(intMissing)
    ln_c(")")
  ln_out()
  if bDetail
    ln_s(string("  detail: k=0 primer by long 0-7 (all reps) "))
    ln_row8(@blkPrim[(rNear - RUN_Q) * BLKN])
    ln_s(string(" | k=0 records right / primer / seed / both / other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_OK])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_PRIM])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_SEED])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_MIX])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runCnt[rNear * NVC + BC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" | k=0 primer records by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[rNear * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | waiting right block "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[rWait])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | disagreeing cells k=0/k=7/waiting "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[rNear])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runDisagree[rFar])
    ln_c("/")
    ln_d(runDisagree[rWait])
    ln_out()

DAT ' ---- Fixed predictions and the run table ----
' Erratum E7: primer cells per repetition at k=0, by delta 0..7
predK0          long    8, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2

' Run table, in run order: arm, shape, kind, copy, no-wait, k, size, lane.
' For arm 1 (SH_F, SH_P) the lane byte is the variant: 0 = FC, 1 = FZ, 2 = FP.
runTab          byte    ARM_P,  SH_R,  KD_NOP,  CP_R_NOP_L,  0, 0, 4, 0      '  0 C1
                byte    ARM_P,  SH_PS, KD_PS,   CP_R_PS,     1, 0, 4, 0      '  1 PS
                byte    ARM_P,  SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF0_L,  1, 0, 4, 0      '  2 T1 k=0
                byte    ARM_P,  SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_L,  1, 7, 4, 0      '  3 T1 k=7
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_F_NOP,    0, 0, 4, 0      '  4 FC N
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_F_RF0,    0, 0, 4, 0      '  5 FC C
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_F_RF0,    1, 0, 4, 0      '  6 FC T
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_F_NOP,    0, 0, 4, 1      '  7 FZ N
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_F_RF0,    0, 0, 4, 1      '  8 FZ C
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_F_RF0,    1, 0, 4, 1      '  9 FZ T
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_P,  KD_NOP,  CP_P_NOP,    0, 0, 4, 2      ' 10 FP N (PTRA++)
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_P,  KD_WAIT, CP_P_RF0,    0, 0, 4, 2      ' 11 FP C
                byte    ARM_FL, SH_P,  KD_TEST, CP_P_RF0,    1, 0, 4, 2      ' 12 FP T
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_FB_NOP,   0, 0, 1, 0      ' 13 RB0 N (value + flags)
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_FB_RF0,   0, 0, 1, 0      ' 14 RB0 C (value + flags)
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_FB_RF0,   1, 0, 1, 0      ' 15 RB0 T k0 (value + flags)
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_B,  1, 7, 1, 0      ' 16 RB0 T k7 (value)
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_FB_NOP,   0, 0, 1, 1      ' 17 RB1
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_FB_RF0,   0, 0, 1, 1
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_FB_RF0,   1, 0, 1, 1
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_B,  1, 7, 1, 1
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_FB_NOP,   0, 0, 1, 2      ' 21 RB2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_FB_RF0,   0, 0, 1, 2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_FB_RF0,   1, 0, 1, 2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_B,  1, 7, 1, 2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_FB_NOP,   0, 0, 1, 3      ' 25 RB3
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_FB_RF0,   0, 0, 1, 3
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_FB_RF0,   1, 0, 1, 3
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_B,  1, 7, 1, 3
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_FW_NOP,   0, 0, 2, 0      ' 29 RW0
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_FW_RF0,   0, 0, 2, 0
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_FW_RF0,   1, 0, 2, 0
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_W,  1, 7, 2, 0
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_FW_NOP,   0, 0, 2, 2      ' 33 RW2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_FW_RF0,   0, 0, 2, 2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_FW_RF0,   1, 0, 2, 2
                byte    ARM_RD, SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_W,  1, 7, 2, 2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_B,  0, 0, 1, 0      ' 37 WB0 N
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_RF1_B,  0, 0, 1, 0      ' 38 WB0 C (W1)
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF1_B,  1, 0, 1, 0      ' 39 WB0 T1
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF2_B,  1, 0, 1, 0      ' 40 WB0 T2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_B,  0, 0, 1, 1      ' 41 WB1
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_RF1_B,  0, 0, 1, 1
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF1_B,  1, 0, 1, 1
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF2_B,  1, 0, 1, 1
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_B,  0, 0, 1, 2      ' 45 WB2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_RF1_B,  0, 0, 1, 2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF1_B,  1, 0, 1, 2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF2_B,  1, 0, 1, 2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_B,  0, 0, 1, 3      ' 49 WB3
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_RF1_B,  0, 0, 1, 3
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF1_B,  1, 0, 1, 3
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF2_B,  1, 0, 1, 3
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_W,  0, 0, 2, 0      ' 53 WW0
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_RF1_W,  0, 0, 2, 0
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF1_W,  1, 0, 2, 0
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF2_W,  1, 0, 2, 0
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_W,  0, 0, 2, 2      ' 57 WW2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_RF1_W,  0, 0, 2, 2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF1_W,  1, 0, 2, 2
                byte    ARM_WR, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_RF2_W,  1, 0, 2, 2
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_F,  KD_NOP,  CP_F_NOP,    0, 0, 4, 0      ' 61 FR N (value + flags)
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_F,  KD_WAIT, CP_F_WF0,    0, 0, 4, 0      ' 62 FR C
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_F_WF0,    1, 0, 4, 0      ' 63 FR T k0
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_F,  KD_TEST, CP_F_WF7,    1, 7, 4, 0      ' 64 FR T k7
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_W,  KD_NOP,  CP_W_NOP_L,  0, 0, 4, 0      ' 65 FW N
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_W,  KD_WAIT, CP_W_WF1_L0, 0, 0, 4, 0      ' 66 FW C (W1 k0)
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_WF1_L0, 1, 0, 4, 0      ' 67 FW T1 k0
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_WF1_L7, 1, 7, 4, 0      ' 68 FW T1 k7
                byte    ARM_WF, SH_W,  KD_TEST, CP_W_WF2_L0, 1, 0, 4, 0      ' 69 FW T2 k0
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_NOP,  CP_B_NOP,    0, 0, 4, 0      ' 70 QB N
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_WAIT, CP_B_RF0,    0, 0, 4, 0      ' 71 QB C
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_TEST, CP_B_RF0,    1, 0, 4, 0      ' 72 QB T k0
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_TEST, CP_B_RF7,    1, 7, 4, 0      ' 73 QB T k7
runTabEnd       byte    0
                alignl

' ===========================================================================
' MEASURING COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).
' No debug(), no BRK, no interrupt in this cog (DEBUG_COGS excludes it).
' From each primer RDLONG to its test instruction there is nothing but the
' RDFAST/WRFAST (or the NOP standing in for it), the k NOPs and (block) the
' SETQ; no ## operand.  Loop variables are grouped (c_cmd..c_tmp); the
' sacrificial block registers and their guard bands end the image.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Cog ----
pasm            mov     c_tmp, ##STAT_READY
                wrlong  c_tmp, ptra[MB_ALIVE]

wait_cmd        rdlong  c_cmd, ptra                     wz      ' MB_CMD: 0 = idle
        if_z    jmp     #wait_cmd
                rdlong  c_copy, ptra[MB_COPY]
                rdlong  c_mode, ptra[MB_MODE]
                rdlong  c_off, ptra[MB_OFF]
                rdlong  c_pa, ptra[MB_PRIM]
                rdlong  c_tb, ptra[MB_TBL]
                rdlong  c_oldv, ptra[MB_OLD]
                rdlong  c_newv, ptra[MB_NEW]
                rdlong  c_flush, ptra[MB_FLUSH]
                alts    c_copy, #vec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0
                mov     c_rp, c_res
                mov     c_reps, #REPS
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_R                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #r_rep
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_F                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #f_rep
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_W                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #w_rep
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_B                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #b_rep
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_SNAP                wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_snap
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_P                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #p_ent
cmd_done        wrlong  c_mode, ptra[MB_ECHO]                   ' epilogue, after every record: echo the mode run
                wrlong  #0, ptra                                ' MB_CMD := 0 -> done
                jmp     #wait_cmd

do_snap        setq    #COG_DUMP_N - 1                         ' arm 5 baseline: cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub
                wrlong  pasm, c_dump
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- settle: >= 200 clocks; arm 4 adds the FIFO flush (blocking RDFAST waits for
'--- any previous WRFAST to finish) and a second settle.  Changes no flag.
settle          mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
s_d1            djnz    c_t, #s_d1
                tjz     c_flush, #s_ret
                rdfast  #0, c_strm                              ' flush: blocking
                mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
s_d2            djnz    c_t, #s_d2
s_ret           ret

'--- image R: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 ar; record (rep*8 + af)*8 + ar
r_rep           mov     c_af, #0
r_af            mov     c_ar, #0
r_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm                            ' stream address: slot bits = af
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tb
                add     c_pr, c_off                             ' test address: slot bits = ar, + byte offset
                mov     c_dst, c_seedv                          ' "never written" stays visible
                jmp     c_vec                                   ' the trial copy
r_settle        call    #settle
                wrlong  c_dst, c_rp                             ' one record per trial
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_af
                djnz    c_reps, #r_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- value + flags (arm 1 FC/FZ, arm 2 k=0 runs, arm 4 image R): as image R; record value, flags
f_rep           mov     c_af, #0
f_af            mov     c_ar, #0
f_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tb
                add     c_pr, c_off                             ' + byte offset (arm 2)
                mov     c_dst, c_seedv
                modcz   _set, _set                      wcz     ' C=1 Z=1: no read gives both
                jmp     c_vec
f_settle        call    #settle
                bitc    c_fl, #FLB_C_LATE                       ' late capture: C
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_LATE                       ' late capture: Z
                wrlong  c_dst, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_fl, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #f_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #f_af
                djnz    c_reps, #f_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- arm 1 PTRA++: as image R with the test read through ptra++; record value,
'--- ptra after minus before.  PTRA holds the mailbox pointer: kept in c_mb.
p_ent           mov     c_mb, ptra                              ' keep the mailbox pointer
p_rep           mov     c_af, #0
p_af            mov     c_ar, #0
p_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tb
                mov     c_dst, c_seedv
                mov     ptra, c_pr                              ' the test pointer, set before the primer
                jmp     c_vec
p_settle        call    #settle
                mov     c_fl, ptra
                sub     c_fl, c_pr                              ' ptra after minus before
                wrlong  c_dst, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_fl, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #p_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #p_af
                djnz    c_reps, #p_rep
                mov     ptra, c_mb                              ' the mailbox pointer back
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image W: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 aw; records rb1, rb2 per trial
w_rep           mov     c_af, #0
w_af            mov     c_ar, #0                                ' c_ar = aw: the target's slot bits
w_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm
                mov     c_pl, c_ar
                shl     c_pl, #2
                add     c_pl, c_tb                              ' the target long (aligned): slot bits = aw
                mov     c_pw, c_pl
                add     c_pw, c_off                             ' the lane written
                wrlong  c_oldv, c_pl                            ' the target holds the old long
                mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
w_d1            djnz    c_t, #w_d1
                mov     c_rb1, c_seedv
                mov     c_rb2, c_seedv
                jmp     c_vec
w_settle        call    #settle
                rdlong  c_rb2, c_pl                             ' read-back after everything settled
                wrlong  c_rb1, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                wrlong  c_rb2, c_rp
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #w_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #w_af
                djnz    c_reps, #w_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- arm 5 block: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 ar; record blk0..blk7 per trial
b_rep           mov     c_af, #0
b_af            mov     c_ar, #0
b_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tb                              ' block start: slot bits = ar
                mov     c_blk0 + 0, c_seedv                     ' the sacrificial range := seed
                mov     c_blk0 + 1, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 2, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 3, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 4, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 5, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 6, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 7, c_seedv
                jmp     c_vec
b_settle        call    #settle
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                wrlong  c_blk0, c_rp                            ' record: the 8 sacrificial longs
                add     c_rp, #BLKN * 4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #b_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #b_af
                djnz    c_reps, #b_rep
                setq    #COG_DUMP_N - 1                         ' integrity: cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub
                wrlong  pasm, c_dump
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image R trial copies: primer, RDFAST/WRFAST (or NOP), k NOPs, the read under test
tc_r_nop_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' primer
                nop                                             ' NOP in place of the RDFAST
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                             ' the RDLONG under test
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_rf0_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_rf7_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_ps         rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' PS: primer
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' PS: the stream under test (no-wait)
                waitx   #STREAM_WAIT                            ' PS: long past any start-up
                rflong  c_dst                                   ' PS: the stream's first long
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_rf7_b      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 2 k=7 (value only)
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdbyte  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_rf7_w      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 2 k=7 (value only)
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdword  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle

'--- value + flags copies: the test read with WCZ; flags captured at once (outside the timed stretch)
tc_f_nop        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 1 FC/FZ N, arm 4 FR N
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz
                wrc     c_fl                                    ' bit 0 := C (rest cleared)
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM                        ' bit 1 := Z
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_f_rf0        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 1 FC/FZ C, T
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_f_wf0        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 4 FR C, T k=0
                wrfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' WRFAST in place of the RDFAST
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_f_wf7        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 4 FR T k=7
                wrfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_fb_nop       rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 2 RDBYTE N
                nop
                rdbyte  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz     ' the RDBYTE under test
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_fb_rf0       rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 2 RDBYTE C, T k=0
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                rdbyte  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_fw_nop       rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 2 RDWORD N
                nop
                rdword  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz     ' the RDWORD under test
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle
tc_fw_rf0       rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' arm 2 RDWORD C, T k=0
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                rdword  c_dst, c_pr                     wcz
                wrc     c_fl
                bitz    c_fl, #FLB_Z_IMM
                jmp     #f_settle

'--- arm 1 PTRA++ copies: the test RDLONG through ptra++ (ptra set before the primer)
tc_p_nop        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, ptra++                           ' the RDLONG under test
                jmp     #p_settle
tc_p_rf0        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                rdlong  c_dst, ptra++
                jmp     #p_settle

'--- image W trial copies: primer, RDFAST/WRFAST (or NOP), k NOPs, the write, read-back (W1) or NOP (W2)
tc_w_nop_b      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                nop
                wrbyte  c_newv, c_pw                            ' the WRBYTE under test
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl                             ' immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_rf1_b      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                wrbyte  c_newv, c_pw
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_rf2_b      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                wrbyte  c_newv, c_pw
                nop                                             ' W2: no immediate read-back
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_nop_w      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                nop
                wrword  c_newv, c_pw                            ' the WRWORD under test
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_rf1_w      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                wrword  c_newv, c_pw
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_rf2_w      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                wrword  c_newv, c_pw
                nop
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_nop_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                nop
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw                            ' the WRLONG under test (arm 4)
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_wf1_l0     rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                wrfast  c_mode, c_pf
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_wf1_l7     rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                wrfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw
                rdlong  c_rb1, c_pl
                jmp     #w_settle
tc_w_wf2_l0     rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                wrfast  c_mode, c_pf
                wrlong  c_newv, c_pw
                nop
                jmp     #w_settle

'--- arm 5 block copies: primer, RDFAST (or NOP), k NOPs, SETQ + the block RDLONG
tc_b_nop        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                nop
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr                            ' the block RDLONG under test
                jmp     #b_settle
tc_b_rf0        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr
                jmp     #b_settle
tc_b_rf7        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr
                jmp     #b_settle

'--- trial-copy vectors (CP_* order)
vec_tab         long    tc_r_nop_l, tc_r_rf0_l, tc_r_rf7_l, tc_r_ps             ' 0..3
                long    tc_r_rf7_b, tc_r_rf7_w                                  ' 4..5
                long    tc_f_nop, tc_f_rf0, tc_f_wf0, tc_f_wf7                  ' 6..9
                long    tc_fb_nop, tc_fb_rf0, tc_fw_nop, tc_fw_rf0              ' 10..13
                long    tc_w_nop_b, tc_w_rf1_b, tc_w_rf2_b                      ' 14..16
                long    tc_w_nop_w, tc_w_rf1_w, tc_w_rf2_w                      ' 17..19
                long    tc_w_nop_l, tc_w_wf1_l0, tc_w_wf1_l7, tc_w_wf2_l0       ' 20..23
                long    tc_b_nop, tc_b_rf0, tc_b_rf7                            ' 24..26
                long    tc_p_nop, tc_p_rf0                                      ' 27..28

'--- cog constants
c_strm          long    HUB_STRM
c_res           long    HUB_RES
c_dump          long    HUB_DUMP
c_seedv         long    SEEDV

'--- loop variables (c_cmd .. c_tmp): excluded from the integrity check
c_cmd           long    0
c_copy          long    0
c_mode          long    0                                       ' FIFO D under test
c_off           long    0
c_pa            long    0
c_tb            long    0
c_oldv          long    0
c_newv          long    0
c_flush         long    0
c_vec           long    0
c_rp            long    0
c_reps          long    0
c_af            long    0
c_ar            long    0
c_pf            long    0
c_pr            long    0
c_pl            long    0
c_pw            long    0
c_dst           long    0
c_fl            long    0
c_rb1           long    0
c_rb2           long    0
c_t             long    0
c_mb            long    0                                       ' PTRA++ runs: the mailbox pointer
c_tmp           long    0

'--- arm 5: guard band, the sacrificial range (written only by the block reads
'--- and their presets), guard band; checked except the sacrificial range
c_guard_lo      long    GUARD_V + 0, GUARD_V + 1, GUARD_V + 2, GUARD_V + 3, GUARD_V + 4, GUARD_V + 5, GUARD_V + 6, GUARD_V + 7
c_blk0          long    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
c_guard_hi      long    GUARD_V + 8, GUARD_V + 9, GUARD_V + 10, GUARD_V + 11, GUARD_V + 12, GUARD_V + 13, GUARD_V + 14, GUARD_V + 15
pasm_end

